window.TWG_I18N=window.TWG_I18N||{};TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]=Object.assign(TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]||{},{"Hi! I'm your beer goat 🍺":"嗨！我是你的啤酒山羊 🍺","I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Beer 1 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"我會為你量身打造一條通過啤酒 1 考試的學習路線，只要回答 5 個簡單問題。","Beer 1 exam":"啤酒 1 考試","Lessons, quizzes and flashcards on beer ingredients, brewing, styles and service.":"關於啤酒原料、釀造、風格與侍酒的課程、測驗和字卡。","Review beer ingredients, styles and terms":"複習啤酒原料、風格與術語","All of Beer 1":"啤酒 1 全部內容","Lessons, flashcards and mistakes: only the Beer 1 syllabus.":"課程、字卡與錯題：只包含啤酒 1 的考試大綱。","Beer 1 games":"啤酒 1 遊戲","Short games on Beer 1 questions and terms.":"用啤酒 1 的題目和術語玩的小遊戲。","What beer is":"啤酒是什麼","Malt and other sugar sources":"麥芽和其他糖源","The brewing steps":"釀造步驟","Hops and other flavourings":"啤酒花和其他調味材料","Tasting beer":"品飲啤酒","Malt-driven styles: base malts only":"麥芽主導的風格：只用基礎麥芽","Malt-driven styles: some speciality malts":"麥芽主導的風格：加入一些特殊麥芽","Hop-driven styles":"啤酒花主導的風格","Yeast-driven styles":"酵母主導的風格","Sour styles":"酸啤酒風格","Storage and faults":"保存與缺陷","Serving beer":"啤酒侍酒","Beer and food":"啤酒與餐點","Ingredients and production":"原料與生產","Storage, service and food":"保存、侍酒與餐點","b14":"b14","What are the four main ingredients of beer?":"啤酒的四種主要原料是什麼？","Malt, water, hops, yeast":"麥芽、水、啤酒花、酵母","Rice, kōji, water, yeast":"米、麴、水、酵母","Malt, sugar, hops, neutral alcohol":"麥芽、糖、啤酒花、中性酒精","Barley, grapes, water, yeast":"大麥、葡萄、水、酵母","Malt, water, hops and yeast are the four main ingredients.":"麥芽、水、啤酒花和酵母是四種主要原料。","Rice and kōji are sake ingredients. Sugar is sometimes used but is not one of the four; grapes belong to wine.":"米和麴是清酒的原料。糖有時會使用，但不是四種之一；葡萄屬於葡萄酒。","During fermentation, yeast turns sugar into alcohol and also produces…":"發酵時，酵母把糖變成酒精，同時還會產生…","carbon dioxide and aromas":"二氧化碳和香氣","starch and enzymes":"澱粉和酵素","hops and colour":"啤酒花和顏色","oxygen and water":"氧氣和水","Yeast creates alcohol, carbon dioxide (CO2) and aromas.":"酵母產生酒精、二氧化碳（CO2）和香氣。","Starch and enzymes come from the malt. Colour mostly comes from malt, and hops are an added ingredient.":"澱粉和酵素來自麥芽。顏色主要來自麥芽，啤酒花則是添加的原料。","A beer is 5% abv. Which alcohol band is it in?":"一款啤酒是 5% abv。它屬於哪個酒精等級？","Low":"低","High":"高","Very high":"非常高","Medium = 4.1–5.9% abv.":"中等 = 4.1–5.9% abv。","Low is up to 4%, high 6–9%, very high above 9%.":"低是 4% 以下，高是 6–9%，非常高是 9% 以上。","Above what alcohol level is a beer 'very high' in alcohol?":"酒精濃度超過多少，啤酒就屬於「非常高」？","Above 9%":"超過 9%","Above 4%":"超過 4%","Above 6%":"超過 6%","Above 15%":"超過 15%","Very high = above 9% abv.":"非常高 = 超過 9% abv。","6–9% is 'high' and 4.1–5.9% 'medium'.":"6–9% 是「高」，4.1–5.9% 是「中等」。","By volume, what is the main ingredient in beer?":"以體積來說，啤酒最主要的原料是什麼？","Malt":"麥芽","Hops":"啤酒花","Water is by far the largest ingredient, so breweries need a reliable supply.":"水是遠遠最大宗的原料，所以酒廠需要可靠的水源。","Malt gives sugar and colour, hops bitterness and aroma, yeast alcohol: but all are far smaller in quantity than water.":"麥芽帶來糖和顏色，啤酒花帶來苦味和香氣，酵母帶來酒精：但分量都遠少於水。","Why were hops originally used in beer?":"啤酒最初為什麼要使用啤酒花？","For their antibacterial properties, to help preserve the beer":"因為它的抗菌特性，有助於保存啤酒","To give a dark colour":"為了讓顏色變深","To provide sugar":"為了提供糖","To create alcohol":"為了產生酒精","Hops were first used to preserve; today they are prized mainly for bitterness and aroma.":"啤酒花最初是用來保存的；如今主要因苦味和香氣而受重視。","Colour and sugar come from malt, alcohol from yeast.":"顏色和糖來自麥芽，酒精來自酵母。","Why can yeast not use the starch in malt directly?":"為什麼酵母不能直接利用麥芽中的澱粉？","Because starch is sugars bonded into long chains":"因為澱粉是糖連結成的長鏈","Because starch is too bitter":"因為澱粉太苦","Because starch is already alcohol":"因為澱粉已經是酒精","Because yeast only eats hops":"因為酵母只吃啤酒花","Yeast can only eat shorter sugars: the starch must first be broken up by enzymes.":"酵母只能吃較短的糖：澱粉必須先被酵素切開。","Starch is neither bitter nor alcoholic, and yeast feeds on sugars, not hops.":"澱粉既不苦也不含酒精，酵母吃的是糖，不是啤酒花。","In beer, where do the enzymes that convert starch to sugar come from?":"在啤酒中，把澱粉轉化成糖的酵素從哪裡來？","The malt":"麥芽","The hops":"啤酒花","Kōji":"麴","The water":"水","Malt supplies both the starch and the enzymes to convert it.":"麥芽同時提供澱粉和轉化它的酵素。","Kōji supplies the enzymes in sake, not beer. Hops and water do not bring conversion enzymes.":"麴是在清酒中提供酵素，不是啤酒。啤酒花和水不帶來轉化酵素。","What are enzymes?":"酵素是什麼？","Substances that speed up reactions, such as starch conversion":"能加速反應的物質，例如澱粉轉化","Types of yeast":"酵母的種類","Hop varieties":"啤酒花品種","Bacteria that make beer sour":"讓啤酒變酸的細菌","Enzymes are catalysts: here they break starch into sugars.":"酵素是催化劑：在這裡它們把澱粉分解成糖。","They are not microorganisms like yeast or bacteria, nor plants like hops.":"它們不是像酵母或細菌那樣的微生物，也不是像啤酒花那樣的植物。","Which grain is the most important for brewers?":"對釀酒師來說，最重要的穀物是哪一種？","Rice":"米","Maize (corn)":"玉米","Sorghum":"高粱","Barley is the most used grain and the one most often malted.":"大麥是最常用、也最常被製成麥芽的穀物。","Rice, maize and sorghum are also used, but as extras.":"米、玉米和高粱也會使用，但只是輔料。","What are the three key steps of malting?":"製麥的三個關鍵步驟是什麼？","Steeping, germination, kilning":"浸麥、發芽、烘麥","Milling, mashing, boiling":"碾磨、糖化、煮沸","Polishing, washing, steaming":"精米、洗米、蒸米","Fermentation, carbonation, packaging":"發酵、充氣、包裝","The grain is soaked, sprouts, and is then dried in a kiln.":"穀物先浸水、發芽，然後在烘麥窯中乾燥。","Milling, mashing, boiling, fermentation and so on are brewing steps, after malting. Polishing applies to sake rice.":"碾磨、糖化、煮沸、發酵等是製麥之後的釀造步驟。精米適用於清酒用米。","What happens during germination?":"發芽時會發生什麼？","The embryo grows and enzymes form inside the grain":"胚芽生長，穀粒內部形成酵素","The grain is roasted until black":"穀物被烘烤到變黑","The yeast makes alcohol":"酵母產生酒精","Hops are added":"加入啤酒花","With water absorbed, the embryo wakes up and produces enzymes.":"吸收水分後，胚芽甦醒並產生酵素。","Roasting comes later, for some speciality malts. Yeast and hops come in at the brewery, not during malting.":"烘烤是之後才進行的，用於某些特殊麥芽。酵母和啤酒花是在酒廠加入，不是在製麥時。","Why must germination be stopped by kilning?":"為什麼必須以烘麥來停止發芽？","Otherwise the embryo would use up the starch":"否則胚芽會把澱粉用光","To create alcohol in the grain":"為了在穀粒中產生酒精","To remove the enzymes":"為了去除酵素","To grow the hops":"為了種植啤酒花","If the grain kept growing, the starch the brewer needs would go into the plant.":"如果穀物繼續生長，釀酒師需要的澱粉就會被植物用掉。","Kilning keeps the enzymes (especially in base malts) rather than removing them, and makes no alcohol.":"烘麥會保留酵素（尤其是基礎麥芽），而不是去除酵素，也不會產生酒精。","Besides stopping germination, what does kilning produce?":"除了停止發芽，烘麥還會產生什麼？","Colour and aromas in the malt":"麥芽的顏色和香氣","Alcohol and carbon dioxide":"酒精和二氧化碳","Hop bitterness":"啤酒花的苦味","Lactic sourness":"乳酸的酸味","Kiln heat creates colour and aromas; more heat, more colour.":"烘麥窯的熱度創造顏色和香氣；熱度越高，顏色越深。","Alcohol and CO2 come from yeast, bitterness from hops, lactic sourness from bacteria.":"酒精和 CO2 來自酵母，苦味來自啤酒花，乳酸酸味來自細菌。","Why are base malts kilned at the lowest temperatures?":"為什麼基礎麥芽用最低的溫度烘麥？","To avoid damaging the enzymes needed in mashing":"避免破壞糖化時需要的酵素","To get a black colour":"為了得到黑色","To give coffee aromas":"為了帶來咖啡香氣","To remove the starch":"為了去除澱粉","Low heat = intact enzymes, ready to convert starch in the mash.":"低溫 = 酵素完好，準備在糖化時轉化澱粉。","Black colour and coffee come from heavily roasted malts with destroyed enzymes. The starch must stay: it is the sugar source.":"黑色和咖啡香氣來自深度烘烤、酵素已被破壞的麥芽。澱粉必須保留：它是糖的來源。","Which aromas do base malts typically give?":"基礎麥芽通常帶來哪些香氣？","Water cracker, bread dough, bread crumb, light honey":"蘇打餅乾、麵團、麵包心、淡淡的蜂蜜","Coffee and chocolate":"咖啡和巧克力","Banana and clove":"香蕉和丁香","Grapefruit and pine":"葡萄柚和松木","Base malts give light bready, cereal aromas and a straw or gold colour.":"基礎麥芽帶來淡淡的麵包、穀物香氣，以及稻草色或金色。","Coffee and chocolate come from roasted speciality malts; banana and clove from yeast; grapefruit and pine from hops.":"咖啡和巧克力來自烘烤的特殊麥芽；香蕉和丁香來自酵母；葡萄柚和松木來自啤酒花。","A beer made with base malts only: what colour will it be?":"只用基礎麥芽釀的啤酒會是什麼顏色？","Straw or gold":"稻草色或金色","Copper":"銅","On their own, base malts give a straw or gold beer.":"單用基礎麥芽，會得到稻草色或金色的啤酒。","Amber, copper, brown and black need speciality malts.":"琥珀色、銅色、棕色和黑色需要特殊麥芽。","How are speciality malts made?":"特殊麥芽是怎麼做的？","By kilning hotter or longer, or by roasting the malt":"以更高溫或更長時間烘麥，或烘烤麥芽","By skipping germination":"省略發芽","By adding hops during malting":"在製麥時加入啤酒花","By boiling the grains":"煮沸穀物","More heat (or roasting) gives more colour and aroma but damages the enzymes.":"更多熱度（或烘烤）帶來更多顏色和香氣，但會破壞酵素。","Germination is part of all malting; hops go in during the boil, not malting.":"發芽是所有製麥的一部分；啤酒花是在煮沸時加入，不是製麥時。","What happens to the enzymes in speciality malts?":"特殊麥芽中的酵素會怎麼樣？","They are damaged or destroyed by the heat":"被高溫破壞或摧毀","They multiply":"大量增加","They turn into yeast":"變成酵母","They stay more active than in base malts":"比基礎麥芽中的更活躍","The high temperatures for speciality malts damage or destroy the enzymes.":"製作特殊麥芽的高溫會破壞或摧毀酵素。","That is why a recipe needs base malt: it brings the enzymes to convert the starch of the whole mash.":"所以配方需要基礎麥芽：它提供轉化整個糖化醪中澱粉的酵素。","Which of these aromas typically comes from a roasted speciality malt?":"下列哪種香氣通常來自烘烤的特殊麥芽？","Coffee":"咖啡","Bread crumb":"麵包心","Grapefruit":"葡萄柚","Clove":"丁香","Coffee and chocolate are aromas of heavily roasted malts.":"咖啡和巧克力是深度烘烤麥芽的香氣。","Bread crumb comes from base malt, grapefruit from hops, clove from yeast.":"麵包心來自基礎麥芽，葡萄柚來自啤酒花，丁香來自酵母。","What effect do rice and maize tend to have in the recipe?":"米和玉米在配方中通常有什麼作用？","Lighter aroma intensity and lighter body":"香氣強度較淡、酒體較輕","More colour and roasted aromas":"更多顏色和烘烤香氣","Creamy texture and haze":"綿密的口感和混濁","More bitterness":"更多苦味","Rice, maize and most sugars and syrups lighten aroma and body.":"米、玉米以及大多數糖和糖漿會讓香氣和酒體變輕。","Creaminess and haze are typical of wheat; roasted colour of speciality malts; bitterness of hops.":"綿密和混濁是小麥的特徵；烘烤的顏色來自特殊麥芽；苦味來自啤酒花。","Which grain can give a smooth, creamy texture and contribute to haze?":"哪種穀物能帶來滑順綿密的口感，並造成混濁？","Maize":"玉米","Heavily roasted barley":"深度烘烤的大麥","Wheat brings smoothness and haze, as in wheat beers.":"小麥帶來滑順感和混濁，就像小麥啤酒一樣。","Rice and maize lighten; roasted barley gives dark colour and coffee aromas.":"米和玉米讓啤酒變輕；烘烤大麥帶來深色和咖啡香氣。","What is the grain bill?":"穀物配方（grain bill）是什麼？","The list of types and amounts of malts and grains in a beer":"一款啤酒所用麥芽和穀物的種類與分量清單","The cost of the grain":"穀物的成本","The list of hops":"啤酒花清單","The amount of yeast":"酵母的分量","It is the cereal recipe: which malts and grains, and in what proportion.":"它是穀物的配方：用哪些麥芽和穀物，比例是多少。","It is not about cost, hops or yeast, only the grains.":"它與成本、啤酒花或酵母無關，只關於穀物。","In a typical recipe, which malt makes up the majority?":"在典型配方中，哪種麥芽占大多數？","A base malt":"基礎麥芽","A black roasted malt":"黑色烘烤麥芽","A caramel malt":"焦糖麥芽","No malt: only sugar":"不用麥芽：只用糖","Base malt brings starch and enzymes; speciality malts are used in small amounts.":"基礎麥芽提供澱粉和酵素；特殊麥芽只用少量。","Black and caramel malts are speciality malts, added in small amounts for colour and aroma.":"黑麥芽和焦糖麥芽都是特殊麥芽，少量添加以增加顏色和香氣。","What is milled malt called?":"碾磨過的麥芽叫什麼？","Wort":"麥汁","Spent grains":"麥渣","The milled grains are called grist.":"碾磨過的穀物稱為碎麥芽（grist）。","Wort is the sugary liquid and spent grains the leftover solids; kōji belongs to sake.":"麥汁是含糖的液體，麥渣是剩下的固體；麴屬於清酒。","Which order of production steps is correct?":"哪個生產步驟順序正確？","Milling, mashing, wort boiling, fermentation, carbonation, packaging":"碾磨、糖化、麥汁煮沸、發酵、充氣、包裝","Mashing, milling, fermentation, boiling, packaging, carbonation":"糖化、碾磨、發酵、煮沸、包裝、充氣","Milling, fermentation, mashing, boiling, carbonation, packaging":"碾磨、發酵、糖化、煮沸、充氣、包裝","Boiling, milling, mashing, fermentation, packaging, carbonation":"煮沸、碾磨、糖化、發酵、包裝、充氣","Mill, mash, boil the wort, ferment, carbonate and package.":"碾磨、糖化、煮沸麥汁、發酵、充氣並包裝。","Yeast cannot ferment before mashing because there is no sugar yet; boiling comes after mashing.":"糖化之前還沒有糖，酵母無法發酵；煮沸在糖化之後。","What happens during mashing?":"糖化時會發生什麼？","Malt enzymes turn starch into sugars in hot water":"麥芽的酵素在熱水中把澱粉變成糖","Yeast turns sugar into alcohol":"酵母把糖變成酒精","Most of the hops are added":"加入大部分的啤酒花","The beer is carbonated":"為啤酒充氣","Grist + hot water: the enzymes convert the starch and the sugar dissolves.":"碎麥芽 + 熱水：酵素轉化澱粉，糖溶解在水中。","Alcohol forms in fermentation; hops go in mainly during the boil; carbonation comes later.":"酒精在發酵時形成；啤酒花主要在煮沸時加入；充氣是之後的事。","At the end of mashing, what is the sugary liquid separated from the solids called?":"糖化結束時，與固體分離的含糖液體叫什麼？","The separated sugary liquid is called wort.":"分離出的含糖液體稱為麥汁。","Mash is the grist-and-water mix before separation; spent grains are the solids left.":"糖化醪是分離前碎麥芽和水的混合物；麥渣是剩下的固體。","What are spent grains?":"麥渣是什麼？","The solids left after the wort is separated":"麥汁分離後剩下的固體","Grains not yet malted":"還沒製成麥芽的穀物","The yeast sediment in the bottle":"瓶中的酵母沉澱","Used hop cones":"用過的啤酒花毬花","They are the solid leftovers of the mash, mainly husks.":"它們是糖化醪剩下的固體，主要是穀殼。","The bottle sediment is yeast from bottle-conditioning; unmalted grain and hops are different things.":"瓶中的沉澱是瓶中二次發酵留下的酵母；未製麥的穀物和啤酒花是不同的東西。","Why is the wort boiled?":"為什麼要煮沸麥汁？","To kill microorganisms and add the hops":"殺死微生物並加入啤酒花","To turn starch into sugar":"把澱粉變成糖","To make the grains germinate":"讓穀物發芽","To create the alcohol":"產生酒精","Boiling makes the beer safe and is when the main hop additions happen.":"煮沸讓啤酒安全，也是主要加入啤酒花的時候。","Conversion happens in mashing, germination in malting, alcohol in fermentation.":"轉化發生在糖化，發芽發生在製麥，酒精產生在發酵。","What happens right after the wort is boiled?":"麥汁煮沸後緊接著會發生什麼？","It is cooled rapidly":"快速冷卻","It is canned":"裝罐","It is milled":"碾磨","It is kept hot for days":"保持高溫好幾天","The wort is cooled quickly to a temperature suitable for the yeast.":"麥汁會快速冷卻到適合酵母的溫度。","Yeast would not survive in boiling wort; milling and packaging are other steps.":"酵母無法在沸騰的麥汁中存活；碾磨和包裝是其他步驟。","At which stage is yeast added?":"酵母在哪個階段加入？","At fermentation, to the cooled wort":"發酵時，加入冷卻的麥汁","At milling":"碾磨時","At mashing":"糖化時","During the boil":"煮沸時","The cooled wort goes into a fermentation vessel, where yeast is added.":"冷卻的麥汁進入發酵槽，在那裡加入酵母。","The boil would kill yeast; at milling and mashing there is no wort ready to ferment yet.":"煮沸會殺死酵母；碾磨和糖化時還沒有可以發酵的麥汁。","What does carbonation do?":"充氣的作用是什麼？","Dissolves carbon dioxide in the beer under pressure":"在加壓下讓二氧化碳溶入啤酒","Adds alcohol":"增加酒精","Removes bitterness":"去除苦味","Colours the beer":"為啤酒上色","Dissolved CO2 gives bubbles in the mouth and foam in the glass.":"溶解的 CO2 在口中形成氣泡，在杯中形成泡沫。","Carbonation changes neither alcohol, bitterness nor colour.":"充氣既不改變酒精，也不改變苦味或顏色。","Where can the CO2 injected to top up carbonation come from?":"用來補充碳酸的 CO2 可以從哪裡來？","Bought in or recovered from earlier fermentations":"購買而來，或從之前的發酵中回收","From boiled hops":"來自煮過的啤酒花","From the brewery air":"來自酒廠的空氣","From the spent grains":"來自麥渣","Bought CO2 or CO2 recovered from earlier fermentations is used.":"使用購買的 CO2 或從之前發酵中回收的 CO2。","Hops, air and spent grains are not CO2 sources for carbonation.":"啤酒花、空氣和麥渣都不是充氣用的 CO2 來源。","What is bottle-conditioning?":"瓶中二次發酵是什麼？","A further fermentation in the sealed bottle, leaving a yeast sediment":"在密封的瓶中再次發酵，留下酵母沉澱","Storing beer in a cellar":"把啤酒存放在地窖","Adding hops in the bottle":"在瓶中加入啤酒花","Pasteurising the bottle":"為酒瓶加熱殺菌","Yeast ferments again in the bottle, creating bubbles and a deposit at the bottom.":"酵母在瓶中再次發酵，產生氣泡並在瓶底留下沉澱。","It is not mere storage, nor a hop addition or heat treatment.":"它不只是存放，也不是加入啤酒花或熱處理。","What are the most widely used beer containers?":"最常用的啤酒容器是什麼？","Cans, bottles, kegs":"罐、瓶、桶","Oak casks and amphorae":"橡木桶和雙耳陶罐","Cartons and pouches":"紙盒和軟袋","Glass demijohns":"玻璃大肚瓶","Cans, bottles and kegs are the main containers.":"罐、瓶和桶是主要的容器。","The other options exist in special cases but are not the usual beer packages.":"其他選項在特殊情況下存在，但不是常見的啤酒包裝。","Which part of the hop plant do brewers use?":"釀酒師使用啤酒花植株的哪個部分？","The cone":"毬花","The root":"根","The leaves":"葉子","The seed":"種子","Hop cones contain the compounds that give bitterness and aroma.":"啤酒花毬花含有帶來苦味和香氣的成分。","Roots, leaves and seeds are not the part used in brewing.":"根、葉和種子都不是釀造使用的部分。","In what form do brewers most often use hops?":"釀酒師最常以什麼形式使用啤酒花？","Pellets of dried, milled and pressed cones":"乾燥、碾碎並壓製的毬花顆粒","Fresh cones straight from the field":"剛從田裡採下的新鮮毬花","Hop syrup":"啤酒花糖漿","Dried leaves":"乾燥的葉子","Pellets are the most common form: they save space.":"顆粒是最常見的形式：節省空間。","Whole dried cones are used, but rarely; fresh cones would soon rot.":"整朵乾燥毬花也會使用，但很少；新鮮毬花很快就會腐爛。","Why are hops packed and refrigerated?":"為什麼啤酒花要包裝並冷藏？","To keep their bitterness and aroma":"保持它的苦味和香氣","To make them germinate":"讓它發芽","To turn them into malt":"把它變成麥芽","To make yeast from them":"用它製作酵母","Cold protects the bitter and aromatic compounds in hops.":"低溫保護啤酒花中的苦味和芳香成分。","Germination is for grains being malted, not hops, which become neither malt nor yeast.":"發芽是針對要製麥的穀物，不是啤酒花；啤酒花既不會變成麥芽，也不會變成酵母。","Which aromas are typical of traditional German, Czech or British hops?":"傳統德國、捷克或英國啤酒花的典型香氣是什麼？","Subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy or fruity":"細微的辛香、花香、草本、泥土或果香","Intense tropical fruit and pine":"強烈的熱帶水果和松木","Traditional European hops are restrained: spice, flowers, herbs, earth, a little fruit.":"傳統歐洲啤酒花很含蓄：辛香、花、草本、泥土，帶一點水果。","Intense tropical and pine notes belong to American, NZ and Australian hops. Coffee and chocolate come from malt, banana and clove from yeast.":"強烈的熱帶和松木調性屬於美國、紐西蘭和澳洲啤酒花。咖啡和巧克力來自麥芽，香蕉和丁香來自酵母。","A brewer wants intense citrus, tropical fruit and pine notes. Which hops are they likely to choose?":"一位釀酒師想要強烈的柑橘、熱帶水果和松木調性。他可能選擇哪種啤酒花？","American, New Zealand or Australian":"美國、紐西蘭或澳洲啤酒花","Traditional German":"傳統德國啤酒花","Traditional Czech":"傳統捷克啤酒花","Traditional British":"傳統英國啤酒花","These hops tend to give intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical or pine aromas.":"這些啤酒花往往帶來強烈的柑橘、核果、熱帶水果或松木香氣。","Traditional German, Czech and British hops are subtler: spice, flowers, herbs, earth.":"傳統德國、捷克和英國啤酒花比較細微：辛香、花、草本、泥土。","When are hops added mainly for BITTERNESS?":"啤酒花主要為了「苦味」時，是在什麼時候加入？","Near the start of the boil":"煮沸開始時","Near the end of the boil":"煮沸接近結束時","During malting":"製麥時","Bitterness needs heat and time, so hops go in early.":"苦味需要熱度和時間，所以啤酒花要早點加入。","Late in the boil and after fermentation hops give mainly aroma. No hops are used in malting.":"煮沸後段和發酵後加入的啤酒花主要帶來香氣。製麥時不使用啤酒花。","Why are aroma hops added near the end of the boil?":"為什麼香氣啤酒花要在煮沸接近結束時加入？","Because aromas escape if boiled too long":"因為煮太久香氣會散失","Because it gives more bitterness that way":"因為這樣會帶來更多苦味","To sterilise it":"為了殺菌","To colour the beer":"為了替啤酒上色","Hop aromas are volatile: a short boil keeps them.":"啤酒花香氣是揮發性的：短時間煮沸能保留它們。","More bitterness comes from boiling longer, i.e. adding early. Hops do not colour beer.":"煮越久苦味越多，也就是早點加入。啤酒花不會替啤酒上色。","What is dry hopping?":"什麼是乾投（dry hopping）？","Adding hops during or after fermentation, for aroma":"在發酵期間或之後加入啤酒花，增加香氣","Drying the hop cones":"乾燥啤酒花毬花","Boiling hops without water":"不加水煮啤酒花","Adding hops at the start of the boil":"在煮沸開始時加入啤酒花","Dry hopping happens at a lower temperature, after the boil, and adds aroma.":"乾投在煮沸之後、較低的溫度下進行，增加香氣。","Drying cones is something else, and hops added at the start of the boil are for bitterness.":"乾燥毬花是另一回事，煮沸開始時加入的啤酒花是為了苦味。","Which flavourings have long been used in certain traditional Belgian styles?":"某些傳統比利時風格長久以來使用哪些調味材料？","Fruit (cherries, raspberries), citrus peel, coriander seed":"水果（櫻桃、覆盆子）、柑橘皮、芫荽籽","Only American hops":"只用美國啤酒花","Oak chips":"橡木片","Fruit, citrus peel and coriander are part of Belgian tradition.":"水果、柑橘皮和芫荽是比利時傳統的一部分。","Kōji belongs to sake; American hops are a modern trend, not Belgian tradition.":"麴屬於清酒；美國啤酒花是現代趨勢，不是比利時傳統。","In most countries, what limits apply to flavourings added to beer?":"在大多數國家，添加到啤酒中的調味材料有什麼限制？","None, as long as it is edible and practical":"沒有限制，只要可食用且實際可行","Only hops are allowed":"只允許啤酒花","Only fruit is allowed":"只允許水果","Only European herbs":"只允許歐洲香草","Pumpkin, honey, chilli or coffee: anything edible and practical can be used.":"南瓜、蜂蜜、辣椒或咖啡：任何可食用、實際可行的東西都能使用。","Hops are the most used, but not the only ones allowed.":"啤酒花最常用，但不是唯一允許的。","What is yeast's main job in beer?":"酵母在啤酒中的主要工作是什麼？","To give bitterness":"帶來苦味","To give colour":"帶來顏色","To convert starch":"轉化澱粉","Yeast turns sugar into alcohol; it can also add aromas.":"酵母把糖變成酒精；也能增加香氣。","Bitterness comes from hops, colour from malt, starch conversion from malt enzymes.":"苦味來自啤酒花，顏色來自麥芽，澱粉轉化來自麥芽的酵素。","Which description fits ale yeast?":"哪一項描述符合艾爾酵母？","Ferments quickly, warmer, with many fruity and spicy aromas":"發酵快、溫度較高，帶有許多果香和辛香","Ferments slowly, cool, with little aroma":"發酵慢、溫度低，香氣少","Used only in spontaneous fermentation":"只用於自然發酵","Makes beer sour":"讓啤酒變酸","Ale yeast is quick, likes relative warmth and can give many aromas.":"艾爾酵母發酵快，喜歡相對溫暖的環境，能帶來許多香氣。","Slow, cool and low-aroma describes lager yeast. Sourness comes from lactic bacteria.":"慢、低溫、香氣少描述的是拉格酵母。酸味來自乳酸菌。","What are beers made with lager yeast called?":"用拉格酵母釀的啤酒叫什麼？","Lagers":"拉格","Ales":"艾爾","Sours":"酸啤酒","Stouts":"司陶特","Lager yeast → lagers; ale yeast → ales.":"拉格酵母 → 拉格；艾爾酵母 → 艾爾。","Stouts are ales; 'sour' refers to acidic styles from bacteria.":"司陶特是艾爾；「酸啤酒」指的是由細菌帶來酸味的風格。","Why do brewers choose a particular ale yeast strain?":"為什麼釀酒師會選擇特定的艾爾酵母菌株？","Each strain creates its own signature set of aromas":"每種菌株都會創造自己獨特的香氣組合","All strains give the same result":"所有菌株結果都一樣","To change the colour":"為了改變顏色","To remove the hops":"為了去除啤酒花","There are many different ale strains: the one with the right aromas for the style is chosen.":"艾爾菌株有很多種：會選擇香氣適合該風格的那一種。","Yeast does not set colour or remove hops.":"酵母不決定顏色，也不會去除啤酒花。","What aromas can Brettanomyces give?":"酒香酵母（Brettanomyces）能帶來什麼香氣？","Ripe pineapple, peach, farmyard, leather, hay, earth":"熟鳳梨、桃子、農舍、皮革、乾草、泥土","Only sourness":"只有酸味","No aroma at all":"完全沒有香氣","Brett gives complex fruity and 'rustic' aromas.":"Brett 帶來複雜的果香和「粗獷」的香氣。","Coffee and chocolate come from roasted malt; sourness mainly from lactic bacteria.":"咖啡和巧克力來自烘烤麥芽；酸味主要來自乳酸菌。","What do lactic acid bacteria bring to beer?":"乳酸菌為啤酒帶來什麼？","Acidity (sourness)":"酸度（酸味）","Bitterness":"苦味","A dark colour":"深色","More alcohol":"更多酒精","Lactic bacteria, as in yoghurt, make beer sour.":"乳酸菌就像優格裡的一樣，會讓啤酒變酸。","Bitterness is from hops, colour from malt, alcohol from yeast.":"苦味來自啤酒花，顏色來自麥芽，酒精來自酵母。","What yeast is nearly all beer made with?":"幾乎所有啤酒都是用哪種酵母釀的？","Cultured yeast, selected and grown in a lab":"培養酵母，在實驗室中篩選並培養","Ambient yeast from the surroundings":"來自周遭環境的野生酵母","Baker's yeast":"麵包酵母","No yeast":"不用酵母","Nearly all beers start from a cultured ale or lager strain.":"幾乎所有啤酒都從培養的艾爾或拉格菌株開始。","Ambient yeast is used only in spontaneous fermentation, which is rare. No yeast, no alcohol.":"環境中的野生酵母只用於自然發酵，而自然發酵很少見。沒有酵母，就沒有酒精。","What is spontaneous fermentation?":"什麼是自然發酵？","No cultured yeast or bacteria are added: ambient ones do the work":"不添加培養的酵母或細菌：由環境中的微生物來發酵","A very fast fermentation":"非常快速的發酵","A fermentation without sugar":"沒有糖的發酵","A fermentation with one lab strain":"使用單一實驗室菌株的發酵","The brewer relies on yeast and bacteria living in and around the brewery.":"釀酒師依靠生活在酒廠內外的酵母和細菌。","One lab strain is the opposite: cultured yeast. The term is not about speed.":"單一實驗室菌株正好相反：那是培養酵母。這個詞與速度無關。","What usually happens in the wort with spontaneous fermentation?":"自然發酵時，麥汁中通常會發生什麼？","Many different types of yeast and bacteria grow":"生長出許多不同種類的酵母和細菌","A single lager strain grows":"只生長出單一拉格菌株","Nothing grows":"什麼都不長","Only kōji mould grows":"只長出麴菌","Without cultured additions, a varied community of microorganisms develops.":"沒有添加培養的微生物，會發展出多樣的微生物群落。","A single strain is typical of cultured yeast; kōji belongs to sake.":"單一菌株是培養酵母的特徵；麴屬於清酒。","Why is a white background used when tasting beer?":"品飲啤酒時為什麼要用白色背景？","To assess the colour":"為了評估顏色","To smell aromas better":"為了更容易聞到香氣","To cool the beer":"為了讓啤酒降溫","To increase the foam":"為了增加泡沫","Holding the glass against white makes the colour easier to judge.":"把杯子放在白色前面，比較容易判斷顏色。","The background has no effect on aroma, temperature or foam.":"背景對香氣、溫度或泡沫都沒有影響。","How is a beer's clarity assessed?":"如何評估啤酒的清澈度？","By looking through the glass towards the light":"透過杯子朝光源看","By smelling the glass":"聞杯子","By tasting a sip":"喝一口","By measuring the temperature":"測量溫度","For clarity, look through the liquid towards the light: clear, hazy or opaque.":"評估清澈度時，透過液體朝光源看：清澈、混濁或不透明。","Nose and palate are other stages; temperature does not show clarity.":"香氣和口感是其他階段；溫度無法顯示清澈度。","Which colour scale does the beer tasting grid use, from palest to darkest?":"啤酒品飲表使用哪個顏色等級，從最淺到最深？","Straw, gold, amber, copper, brown, black":"稻草色、金色、琥珀色、銅色、棕色、黑色","Gold, straw, copper, amber, black, brown":"金色、稻草色、銅色、琥珀色、黑色、棕色","Lemon, gold, amber, brown":"檸檬色、金色、琥珀色、棕色","Pink, red, garnet, tawny":"粉紅色、紅色、石榴紅、茶色","The scale runs from straw to black, via gold, amber, copper and brown.":"色階從稻草色到黑色，中間經過金色、琥珀色、銅色和棕色。","The other scales are out of order or belong to wine tasting.":"其他色階順序錯誤，或屬於葡萄酒品飲。","Which of these aromas typically comes from YEAST?":"下列哪種香氣通常來自「酵母」？","Bread crust":"麵包皮","Pine":"松木","Spice notes such as clove and peppercorn come from yeast.":"丁香和胡椒粒等辛香調性來自酵母。","Bread crust and coffee come from malt, pine from hops.":"麵包皮和咖啡來自麥芽，松木來自啤酒花。","Which aroma family comes from HOPS?":"哪一類香氣來自「啤酒花」？","Citrus, tropical fruit, floral, herbal, pine":"柑橘、熱帶水果、花香、草本、松木","Bread, biscuit, caramel":"麵包、餅乾、焦糖","Banana, bubblegum, nail varnish":"香蕉、泡泡糖、去光水","Raisin, prune, date":"葡萄乾、黑棗、椰棗","Hops give floral, fruity (citrus, tropical…), herbal and pine notes.":"啤酒花帶來花香、果香（柑橘、熱帶…）、草本和松木調性。","Bread, caramel and dried fruit come from malt; banana, bubblegum and nail varnish from yeast.":"麵包、焦糖和果乾來自麥芽；香蕉、泡泡糖和去光水來自酵母。","Besides aromas, what is assessed on the palate?":"除了香氣，口感上還要評估什麼？","Intensity, carbonation, body, alcohol, bitterness, sweetness, acidity":"強度、碳酸感、酒體、酒精、苦味、甜度、酸度","Only colour":"只有顏色","Height of the foam":"泡沫的高度","On the palate you judge structure and sensations as well as aromas.":"在口中，除了香氣，還要判斷結構和感受。","Colour, foam and clarity belong to appearance.":"顏色、泡沫和清澈度屬於外觀。","What colour is a beer made only with base malts usually?":"只用基礎麥芽釀的啤酒通常是什麼顏色？","Base malts give straw or gold beers.":"基礎麥芽釀出稻草色或金色的啤酒。","Darker colours need speciality malts.":"較深的顏色需要特殊麥芽。","What effect does using rice, sugar or syrup have in a pale lager?":"在淡色拉格中使用米、糖或糖漿有什麼影響？","Lighter aroma intensity and body":"香氣強度和酒體較輕","A darker colour":"顏色更深","More sourness":"更酸","Compared with an all-malt beer, the result is lighter and less aromatic.":"與全麥芽啤酒相比，結果更輕盈、香氣較少。","Colour, bitterness and sourness do not depend on these ingredients.":"顏色、苦味和酸味都不取決於這些原料。","Which description fits an American or international pale lager?":"哪一項描述符合美式或國際淡色拉格？","Straw or gold, light aroma, low-medium bitterness, high carbonation":"稻草色或金色，香氣淡，苦味中低，碳酸感強","Black, coffee and chocolate, very high alcohol":"黑色，咖啡和巧克力，酒精非常高","Hazy, banana and clove":"混濁，香蕉和丁香","Sour with farmyard aromas":"酸，帶有農舍香氣","It is the world's most popular easy-drinking pale beer.":"它是全世界最受歡迎、易飲的淡色啤酒。","The others describe stout, weissbier and sour beers such as geuze.":"其他選項描述的是司陶特、德式小麥啤酒和貴茲等酸啤酒。","What does 'hell' mean in Munich helles?":"慕尼黑淡色拉格（Munich helles）的「hell」是什麼意思？","Bright, light or pale":"明亮、淺色或淡色","Strong":"強烈","'Hell' is German for bright or pale: helles is a gold lager.":"「Hell」是德文的明亮或淡色：helles 是金色的拉格。","'Dunkel' means dark and 'Weizen' wheat.":"「Dunkel」是深色，「Weizen」是小麥。","Munich helles is…":"慕尼黑淡色拉格是…","a gold lager with bread-crumb malt and subtle hops":"帶有麵包心麥芽香和細微啤酒花的金色拉格","a heavily roasted black ale":"深度烘烤的黑色艾爾","a hazy wheat ale":"混濁的小麥艾爾","a spontaneously fermented sour beer":"自然發酵的酸啤酒","Gold lager, bread crumb or cracker, subtle hop notes, low-medium bitterness, medium alcohol.":"金色拉格，麵包心或餅乾，細微的啤酒花調性，苦味中低，酒精中等。","It is a lager, not an ale, and is neither dark, hazy nor sour.":"它是拉格不是艾爾，既不深色、不混濁，也不酸。","Which base-malt-only malt-driven style is an ALE?":"只用基礎麥芽、麥芽主導的風格中，哪一個是「艾爾」？","International pale lager":"國際淡色拉格","Blonde (golden) ale is the ale of the group, next to two lagers.":"金色艾爾（Blonde／golden ale）是這組中的艾爾，另外兩個是拉格。","Helles and international lager are lagers; dunkel is a lager with speciality malts.":"淡色拉格（helles）和國際拉格是拉格；深色拉格（dunkel）是使用特殊麥芽的拉格。","What other name is blonde ale sometimes labelled with?":"金色艾爾（blonde ale）有時會以什麼其他名稱標示？","Blonde ale and golden ale name the same easy, gold style.":"Blonde ale 和 golden ale 指的是同一種易飲的金色風格。","'Blanche' is witbier; brown ale and barley wine use speciality malts.":"「Blanche」是比利時白啤酒；棕色艾爾和大麥酒使用特殊麥芽。","Which description fits a blonde ale?":"哪一項描述符合金色艾爾？","Straw to gold ale, subtle bread crumb, medium bitterness, low to medium alcohol":"稻草色到金色的艾爾，細微的麵包心香，苦味中等，酒精低到中等","Copper lager with toasted nut":"帶有烤堅果香的銅色拉格","Black ale with coffee, very high alcohol":"帶有咖啡香、酒精非常高的黑色艾爾","Hazy, sour wheat beer":"混濁、酸的小麥啤酒","An easy-drinking ale: pale, gently malty, medium bitterness.":"一款易飲的艾爾：淡色、溫和的麥芽香、苦味中等。","A toasty copper lager suggests Munich dunkel, black with coffee an imperial stout, hazy and sour a Berliner weisse.":"帶烘烤感的銅色拉格讓人想到慕尼黑深色拉格，黑色帶咖啡香是帝國司陶特，混濁又酸是柏林白啤酒。","What do international pale lager, Munich helles and blonde ale have in common?":"國際淡色拉格、慕尼黑淡色拉格和金色艾爾有什麼共同點？","They are brewed with base malts only":"它們只用基礎麥芽釀造","They are all ales":"它們都是艾爾","They use dark roasted malts":"它們使用深色烘烤麥芽","They are all sour":"它們都是酸的","Three pale malt-driven styles, straw to gold, made with base malts only.":"三種淡色、麥芽主導的風格，稻草色到金色，只用基礎麥芽釀造。","Two are lagers and only blonde ale is an ale. Roasted malts would give dark colours, and none of the three is a sour style.":"兩個是拉格，只有金色艾爾是艾爾。烘烤麥芽會帶來深色，而且三者都不是酸啤酒風格。","What does 'dunkel' mean?":"「dunkel」是什麼意思？","Double":"雙倍","'Dunkel' is German for dark.":"「Dunkel」是德文的深色。","Pale is 'hell', white is 'weiss'; 'double' recalls dubbel.":"淡色是「hell」，白色是「weiss」；「雙倍」讓人想到 dubbel。","Which description fits Munich dunkel?":"哪一項描述符合慕尼黑深色拉格？","Copper-brown lager with toast and toasted nut":"銅色到棕色的拉格，帶有烤麵包和烤堅果香","Black ale with coffee and very high alcohol":"帶有咖啡香、酒精非常高的黑色艾爾","Very bitter straw lager":"非常苦的稻草色拉格","Hazy ale with coriander":"帶有芫荽的混濁艾爾","A dark lager with speciality malts: toast, bread crust, nut, sometimes caramel or chocolate.":"使用特殊麥芽的深色拉格：烤麵包、麵包皮、堅果，有時有焦糖或巧克力。","The second describes an imperial stout, the third a pilsner, the fourth a witbier.":"第二項描述的是帝國司陶特，第三項是皮爾森，第四項是比利時白啤酒。","What is true of bitterness and alcohol in brown ale?":"關於棕色艾爾的苦味和酒精，哪一項正確？","Both range from low to high":"兩者都從低到高都有","They are always very high":"一定非常高","Bitterness is always absent":"一定沒有苦味","Alcohol always under 4%":"酒精一定低於 4%","Brown ale is a broad style: bitterness and alcohol vary a lot.":"棕色艾爾是範圍很廣的風格：苦味和酒精差異很大。","Options with 'always' are too rigid for this style.":"帶有「一定」的選項對這個風格來說太死板。","Which malt aromas are typical of porter and stout?":"哪些麥芽香氣是波特和司陶特的典型？","Bread crumb and water cracker":"麵包心和蘇打餅乾","Grapefruit and rhubarb":"葡萄柚和大黃","Roasted malts give coffee, chocolate and sometimes caramel, with a brown or black colour.":"烘烤麥芽帶來咖啡、巧克力，有時有焦糖，以及棕色或黑色。","Crumb and cracker are base-malt notes; banana and clove come from yeast; grapefruit and rhubarb suit geuze.":"麵包心和餅乾是基礎麥芽的調性；香蕉和丁香來自酵母；葡萄柚和大黃適合貴茲。","What does 'imperial' usually indicate in a stout's name?":"司陶特名稱中的「imperial」（帝國）通常代表什麼？","Very high alcohol and pronounced roasted aromas":"酒精非常高，烘烤香氣明顯","A beer made in England":"在英格蘭釀造的啤酒","An alcohol-free beer":"無酒精啤酒","A sour beer":"酸啤酒","'Imperial' versions are very strong and strongly roasted.":"「帝國」版本非常烈，烘烤感也很強。","The term shows neither origin, sourness nor absence of alcohol.":"這個詞既不表示產地、酸味，也不表示無酒精。","Which description fits barley wine?":"哪一項描述符合大麥酒（barley wine）？","Often amber ale, intense malt, full body, sweet, high or very high alcohol":"常為琥珀色艾爾，麥芽香濃烈，酒體飽滿，甜，酒精高或非常高","A wine made from barley":"用大麥做的葡萄酒","A light, dry lager":"清淡、不甜的拉格","A sour wheat beer":"酸的小麥啤酒","Despite the name it is a beer: a rich, sweet, strong ale.":"雖然名字這樣叫，它是啤酒：一款濃郁、甜而烈的艾爾。","It is not wine, lager or a sour beer.":"它不是葡萄酒、拉格或酸啤酒。","Which malt-driven style is often suitable for ageing?":"哪種麥芽主導的風格常常適合陳放？","Rich, strong barley wine is often suitable for ageing.":"濃郁而烈的大麥酒常常適合陳放。","Pale lagers, helles and blonde ales are fresh beers best drunk young.":"淡色拉格、慕尼黑淡色拉格和金色艾爾是新鮮的啤酒，最好趁年輕喝。","A black beer with coffee and chocolate aromas: which style is most likely?":"一款帶有咖啡和巧克力香氣的黑色啤酒：最可能是哪種風格？","Porter or stout":"波特或司陶特","Black colour and roasted aromas point to porter or stout.":"黑色和烘烤香氣指向波特或司陶特。","Helles, hazy IPA and Berliner weisse are pale, straw to gold.":"慕尼黑淡色拉格、霧濁 IPA 和柏林白啤酒都是淡色的，稻草色到金色。","Which malt-driven style brewed with speciality malts is a LAGER?":"使用特殊麥芽、麥芽主導的風格中，哪一個是「拉格」？","Munich dunkel is the lager of the group; the others are ales.":"慕尼黑深色拉格是這組中的拉格；其他是艾爾。","Brown ale, porter, stout and barley wine are all ales, fermented with ale yeast.":"棕色艾爾、波特、司陶特和大麥酒都是艾爾，用艾爾酵母發酵。","Which malt aromas are typical of a brown ale?":"哪些麥芽香氣是棕色艾爾的典型？","Toasted nut and toasted bread, sometimes chocolate or caramel":"烤堅果和烤麵包，有時有巧克力或焦糖","Bread dough and water cracker":"麵團和蘇打餅乾","Farmyard and rhubarb":"農舍和大黃","Speciality malts give brown ale its toasty, nutty notes.":"特殊麥芽讓棕色艾爾帶有烘烤、堅果調性。","Banana and clove come from weissbier yeast; bread dough and cracker from base malts alone; farmyard and rhubarb suggest geuze.":"香蕉和丁香來自德式小麥啤酒的酵母；麵團和餅乾只來自基礎麥芽；農舍和大黃讓人想到貴茲。","How is pronounced bitterness with restrained hop aroma achieved?":"如何做到苦味明顯、但啤酒花香氣含蓄？","Most hops early in the boil and few at the end":"大部分啤酒花在煮沸初期加入，最後只加少量","Dry hopping only":"只用乾投","No hops at all":"完全不用啤酒花","All hops at the end of the boil":"所有啤酒花都在煮沸最後加入","Early hops = bitterness; few late hops = little aroma.":"早加啤酒花 = 苦味；後段少量啤酒花 = 香氣少。","Dry hopping and late hops mainly give aroma, not bitterness.":"乾投和後段加入的啤酒花主要帶來香氣，不是苦味。","Which style is a hop-driven lager with traditional hops?":"哪種風格是使用傳統啤酒花、啤酒花主導的拉格？","Traditional Czech or German pilsner":"傳統捷克或德國皮爾森","Czech or German pilsner is the lager of the traditional hop-driven group.":"捷克或德國皮爾森是傳統啤酒花主導組中的拉格。","Bitter is an ale, American IPA uses New World hops, dunkel is malt-driven.":"英式苦啤是艾爾，美式 IPA 使用新世界啤酒花，深色拉格是麥芽主導的。","Which description fits traditional Czech or German pilsner?":"哪一項描述符合傳統捷克或德國皮爾森？","Straw-gold, subtle spicy or floral hops, medium-high bitterness":"稻草色到金色，細微的辛香或花香啤酒花，苦味中高","Hazy, very tropical, little bitterness":"混濁，熱帶風味非常強，苦味少","Black, roasted, very high alcohol":"黑色，烘烤，酒精非常高","Sour, with raspberry syrup":"酸，加覆盆子糖漿","Bread dough or light honey, subtle hops, medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol.":"麵團或淡淡的蜂蜜，細微的啤酒花，苦味中等到高，酒精中等。","The others describe hazy IPA, imperial stout and Berliner weisse.":"其他選項描述的是霧濁 IPA、帝國司陶特和柏林白啤酒。","Which country does bitter come from originally?":"英式苦啤（bitter）最初來自哪個國家？","England":"英格蘭","Bitter is a hop-driven ale from England.":"英式苦啤是來自英格蘭、啤酒花主導的艾爾。","Germany and Belgium are linked to other styles (helles, dubbel…); the USA to APA and American IPA.":"德國和比利時與其他風格有關（慕尼黑淡色拉格、比利時雙料…）；美國則與 APA 和美式 IPA 有關。","Which description fits bitter?":"哪一項描述符合英式苦啤？","Amber-copper ale, biscuit or caramel, subtle hops, medium-high bitterness":"琥珀色到銅色的艾爾，餅乾或焦糖，細微的啤酒花，苦味中高","Straw lager with intense tropical hops":"帶有強烈熱帶啤酒花香的稻草色拉格","Hazy wheat ale with banana":"帶有香蕉香的混濁小麥艾爾","Very sweet black lager":"非常甜的黑色拉格","Bitter pairs toasty, caramel malt with subtle traditional hops.":"英式苦啤結合烘烤、焦糖的麥芽和細微的傳統啤酒花。","Bitter is an ale, not a lager, and has no banana aromas.":"英式苦啤是艾爾不是拉格，也沒有香蕉香氣。","How are high bitterness AND intense hop aromas achieved?":"如何同時做到高苦味「和」強烈的啤酒花香氣？","Hops early in the boil, later on, and dry hopping":"煮沸初期加啤酒花，之後再加，並且乾投","Only early hops":"只在初期加啤酒花","Only speciality malts":"只用特殊麥芽","Spontaneous fermentation":"自然發酵","Early for bitterness, late for flavour and dry hopping for aroma.":"初期加入帶來苦味，後段帶來風味，乾投帶來香氣。","Early hops alone give bitterness with little aroma; malts and spontaneous fermentation are unrelated.":"只在初期加啤酒花會帶來苦味但香氣少；麥芽和自然發酵無關。","Which style is sometimes labelled 'APA'?":"哪種風格有時標示為「APA」？","German pilsner":"德國皮爾森","APA stands for American pale ale.":"APA 是 American pale ale（美式淡色艾爾）的縮寫。","IPA means India pale ale; pilsner and blonde ale do not use this abbreviation.":"IPA 是 India pale ale（印度淡色艾爾）的意思；皮爾森和金色艾爾不使用這個縮寫。","How can American IPA be described compared with American pale ale?":"與美式淡色艾爾相比，美式 IPA 可以怎麼描述？","Stronger, with even more bitterness and hop aroma":"更烈，苦味和啤酒花香氣更強","Lighter and less bitter":"更清淡、苦味較少","Darker and more roasted":"顏色更深、烘烤感更強","More sour":"更酸","American IPA is like a stronger, more bitter, more aromatic APA.":"美式 IPA 就像更烈、更苦、更香的 APA。","Colour stays gold to amber, with no roast or sourness.":"顏色維持金色到琥珀色，沒有烘烤感或酸味。","Which hop aromas define American IPA?":"哪些啤酒花香氣定義了美式 IPA？","Pine, resin, citrus, tropical and stone fruit":"松木、樹脂、柑橘、熱帶水果和核果","Subtle spicy, herbal, earthy":"細微的辛香、草本、泥土","New World hops: pine, resin, citrus, tropical and stone fruit.":"新世界啤酒花：松木、樹脂、柑橘、熱帶水果和核果。","Subtle spicy and earthy notes are traditional European hops; banana and clove come from yeast; coffee and chocolate from malt.":"細微的辛香和泥土調性屬於傳統歐洲啤酒花；香蕉和丁香來自酵母；咖啡和巧克力來自麥芽。","Compared with an American IPA, a hazy IPA is typically…":"與美式 IPA 相比，霧濁 IPA 通常…","less bitter":"苦味較低","more bitter":"苦味較高","darker":"顏色較深","more sour":"較酸","Hazy IPA has low to medium bitterness: it focuses on aroma.":"霧濁 IPA 的苦味低到中等：重點放在香氣。","It is straw or gold, not dark, and not a sour style.":"它是稻草色或金色，不是深色，也不是酸啤酒風格。","What other name is hazy IPA labelled with?":"霧濁 IPA 還會以什麼名稱標示？","Hazy IPA and New England IPA are the same style.":"霧濁 IPA（Hazy IPA）和新英格蘭 IPA（New England IPA）是同一種風格。","Golden ale is another name for blonde ale; imperial stout is a very strong stout.":"Golden ale 是 blonde ale 的另一個名稱；帝國司陶特是非常烈的司陶特。","A straw-coloured, distinctly hazy beer with lots of tropical fruit and moderate bitterness: which style?":"一款稻草色、明顯混濁、帶有大量熱帶水果香、苦味適中的啤酒：是哪種風格？","Hazy + tropical hops + low-medium bitterness = hazy IPA.":"混濁 + 熱帶啤酒花 + 苦味中低 = 霧濁 IPA。","Weissbier is also hazy, but its aromas are yeast-driven banana and clove. Bitter and helles are clear.":"德式小麥啤酒也是混濁的，但它的香氣是酵母帶來的香蕉和丁香。英式苦啤和慕尼黑淡色拉格是清澈的。","Which description fits an American pale ale?":"哪一項描述符合美式淡色艾爾？","Gold to amber ale, citrus or pine hops, medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol":"金色到琥珀色的艾爾，柑橘或松木啤酒花香，苦味中等到高，酒精中等","Straw lager with subtle floral hops":"帶有細微花香啤酒花的稻草色拉格","Black ale with roasted malt":"使用烘烤麥芽的黑色艾爾","Hazy ale with coriander and orange peel":"帶有芫荽和橙皮的混濁艾爾","American hops to the fore, subtle malt, medium to high bitterness.":"美國啤酒花當道，麥芽細微，苦味中等到高。","The straw lager with subtle hops is a pilsner, the black ale a stout, the one with coriander and orange a witbier.":"啤酒花細微的稻草色拉格是皮爾森，黑色艾爾是司陶特，帶芫荽和柳橙的是比利時白啤酒。","What do bitter, American pale ale, American IPA and hazy IPA have in common?":"英式苦啤、美式淡色艾爾、美式 IPA 和霧濁 IPA 有什麼共同點？","They are hop-driven ales":"它們是啤酒花主導的艾爾","They are all lagers":"它們都是拉格","They are sour styles":"它們是酸啤酒風格","They use only traditional European hops":"它們只用傳統歐洲啤酒花","Four hop-driven ales; among the hop-driven styles only pilsner is a lager.":"四種啤酒花主導的艾爾；在啤酒花主導的風格中，只有皮爾森是拉格。","Bitter uses traditional hops, but the three American styles use American, Australian or New Zealand hops. None is a sour style.":"英式苦啤使用傳統啤酒花，但三種美式風格使用美國、澳洲或紐西蘭啤酒花。沒有一種是酸啤酒風格。","Why are yeast-driven styles all ales?":"為什麼酵母主導的風格都是艾爾？","Because lagers typically have few yeast aromas":"因為拉格通常酵母香氣很少","Because lagers contain no yeast":"因為拉格不含酵母","Because ales have no hops":"因為艾爾沒有啤酒花","Because of the law":"因為法律規定","Lager yeast gives little aroma; ale yeast gives a lot, fruity and spicy.":"拉格酵母帶來的香氣很少；艾爾酵母帶來很多果香和辛香。","Lagers are made with yeast too, and ales use hops; no law is involved.":"拉格也是用酵母釀的，艾爾也使用啤酒花；與法律無關。","Which yeast aromas characterise weissbier?":"哪些酵母香氣是德式小麥啤酒的特徵？","Pine and resin":"松木和樹脂","Farmyard and leather":"農舍和皮革","Banana (fruity) and clove (spicy) come from weissbier yeast.":"香蕉（果香）和丁香（辛香）來自德式小麥啤酒的酵母。","Pine and resin are hops, coffee and chocolate roasted malt, farmyard and leather typical of Brett.":"松木和樹脂來自啤酒花，咖啡和巧克力來自烘烤麥芽，農舍和皮革是 Brett 的典型香氣。","What is weissbier also known as?":"德式小麥啤酒（Weissbier）還有什麼名稱？","Weissbier and hefeweizen are the same German wheat beer.":"Weissbier 和 hefeweizen 是同一種德國小麥啤酒。","'Blanche' is witbier, 'dunkel' a dark lager, 'gueuze' a sour beer.":"「Blanche」是比利時白啤酒，「dunkel」是深色拉格，「gueuze」是酸啤酒。","What do 'Weiss' and 'Weizen' mean?":"「Weiss」和「Weizen」是什麼意思？","White and wheat":"白色和小麥","Pale and dark":"淡色和深色","Double and triple":"雙倍和三倍","Yeast and hops":"酵母和啤酒花","Weiss = white, Weizen = wheat: both name wheat beers in Germany.":"Weiss = 白色，Weizen = 小麥：兩者在德國都是指小麥啤酒。","Pale and dark are 'hell' and 'dunkel'; double and triple recall dubbel and tripel.":"淡色和深色是「hell」和「dunkel」；雙倍和三倍讓人想到 dubbel 和 tripel。","Which added flavourings characterise witbier?":"哪些添加的調味材料是比利時白啤酒的特徵？","Coriander seed and orange peel":"芫荽籽和橙皮","Coffee and vanilla":"咖啡和香草","Pumpkin and cinnamon":"南瓜和肉桂","Raspberry syrup":"覆盆子糖漿","Coriander and orange peel give witbier citrus and floral notes.":"芫荽和橙皮讓比利時白啤酒帶有柑橘和花香調性。","Raspberry syrup is sometimes added to Berliner weisse when served.":"覆盆子糖漿有時會在侍酒時加進柏林白啤酒。","Which French term is sometimes on a witbier label?":"比利時白啤酒的酒標上有時會出現哪個法文詞？","'Blanche' means 'white', like 'wit' in Dutch.":"「Blanche」的意思是「白色」，就像荷蘭文的「wit」。","Saison is another yeast-driven style; 'brune' and 'ambrée' describe colours.":"Saison 是另一種酵母主導的風格；「brune」和「ambrée」描述的是顏色。","Which description fits dubbel?":"哪一項描述符合比利時雙料（dubbel）？","Copper-brown, apple, plum, clove, high alcohol, sediment":"銅色到棕色，蘋果、李子、丁香，酒精高，有沉澱","Gold, orange, banana, very high alcohol":"金色，柳橙、香蕉，酒精非常高","Straw, sour, low alcohol":"稻草色，酸，酒精低","Black, coffee, imperial":"黑色，咖啡，帝國","Dubbel pairs yeast fruit and spice with toast, caramel and dried fruit.":"比利時雙料結合酵母帶來的果香和辛香，以及烤麵包、焦糖和果乾。","The second is tripel, the third Berliner weisse, the fourth an imperial stout.":"第二項是比利時三料，第三項是柏林白啤酒，第四項是帝國司陶特。","Between dubbel and tripel, which usually has more alcohol, and what colour is it?":"比利時雙料和三料之中，哪一個通常酒精較高？是什麼顏色？","Tripel, gold":"三料，金色","Dubbel, brown":"雙料，棕色","Tripel, black":"三料，黑色","They have the same alcohol":"兩者酒精相同","Tripel is gold with high or very high alcohol, even higher than dubbel.":"比利時三料是金色，酒精高或非常高，甚至比雙料更高。","Dubbel is copper-brown but less strong; tripel is not black.":"比利時雙料是銅色到棕色，但沒那麼烈；三料不是黑色的。","Which aromas characterise tripel?":"哪些香氣是比利時三料（tripel）的特徵？","Orange, banana, pepper, clove from yeast; light honey":"酵母帶來的柳橙、香蕉、胡椒、丁香；淡淡的蜂蜜","Roasted coffee and chocolate":"烘烤的咖啡和巧克力","Intense pine and resin":"強烈的松木和樹脂","Vinegar and rancid butter":"醋和腐敗的奶油","In tripel, yeast fruit and spice dominate over light malt.":"在比利時三料中，酵母帶來的果香和辛香蓋過輕盈的麥芽。","Vinegar and rancid butter are bacterial-infection faults. Coffee and pine are not typical of tripel.":"醋和腐敗的奶油是細菌感染造成的缺陷。咖啡和松木不是比利時三料的典型香氣。","Which yeast-driven style can be slightly sour?":"哪種酵母主導的風格可能帶有輕微酸味？","Fruity, peppery saison can be slightly sour.":"帶果香和胡椒味的賽森（saison）可能帶有輕微酸味。","Weissbier, tripel and dubbel are not described as sour.":"德式小麥啤酒、比利時三料和雙料都不會被描述為酸的。","What do dubbel, tripel and saison usually share?":"比利時雙料、三料和賽森通常有什麼共同點？","Sediment from bottle-conditioning and high carbonation":"瓶中二次發酵的沉澱和高碳酸感","Black colour":"黑色","Lager yeast":"拉格酵母","They are highly carbonated ales, often bottle-conditioned with sediment.":"它們是碳酸感高的艾爾，常經瓶中二次發酵而有沉澱。","They are ales, not lagers, and neither black nor spontaneously fermented.":"它們是艾爾不是拉格，既不是黑色，也不是自然發酵。","Which description fits a weissbier?":"哪一項描述符合德式小麥啤酒？","Hazy, straw to gold, banana and clove, low bitterness, high carbonation":"混濁，稻草色到金色，香蕉和丁香，苦味低，碳酸感高","Clear, copper, very bitter":"清澈，銅色，非常苦","Black, roasted, almost flat":"黑色，烘烤，幾乎沒有氣泡","Gold, sour, with farmyard notes":"金色，酸，帶有農舍調性","Yeast gives banana and clove; wheat brings haze and bread-crumb notes.":"酵母帶來香蕉和丁香；小麥帶來混濁和麵包心調性。","A weissbier is never very bitter: its bitterness is low. Gold, sour and farmyard describes geuze.":"德式小麥啤酒從不會非常苦：它的苦味低。金色、酸、農舍描述的是貴茲。","Which grain gives weissbier and witbier their bread-crumb notes and adds to the haze?":"哪種穀物讓德式小麥啤酒和比利時白啤酒帶有麵包心調性，並增加混濁？","They are wheat beers: 'Weizen' actually means wheat.":"它們是小麥啤酒：「Weizen」的意思就是小麥。","Rice and maize lighten aroma and body rather than adding haze. Sorghum is another brewing grain, but not for these styles.":"米和玉米讓香氣和酒體變輕，而不是增加混濁。高粱是另一種釀酒穀物，但不用於這些風格。","Which description fits a saison?":"哪一項描述符合賽森？","Gold to amber, fruity and peppery yeast, medium bitterness, highly carbonated":"金色到琥珀色，帶果香和胡椒味的酵母，苦味中等，碳酸感高","Black and roasted, very high alcohol":"黑色、烘烤，酒精非常高","Straw lager with light aroma":"香氣清淡的稻草色拉格","Saison is a yeast-driven ale: fruit, pepper, lots of bubbles, sometimes a slight sourness.":"賽森是酵母主導的艾爾：果香、胡椒、大量氣泡，有時帶輕微酸味。","Saison is neither a lager nor black. Its alcohol can range from low to high.":"賽森既不是拉格，也不是黑色的。它的酒精可以從低到高。","What bitterness and alcohol does a witbier usually have?":"比利時白啤酒的苦味和酒精通常是多少？","Low bitterness, medium alcohol":"苦味低，酒精中等","High bitterness, high alcohol":"苦味高，酒精高","No bitterness, very high alcohol":"沒有苦味，酒精非常高","High bitterness, low alcohol":"苦味高，酒精低","Witbier is a gentle wheat beer: low in bitterness, medium in alcohol.":"比利時白啤酒是溫和的小麥啤酒：苦味低，酒精中等。","High bitterness marks hop-driven styles such as American IPA; very high alcohol is found in tripel or barley wine, for example.":"高苦味是美式 IPA 等啤酒花主導風格的特徵；非常高的酒精則見於例如比利時三料或大麥酒。","Where does the sour character of sour styles come from?":"酸啤酒風格的酸味從哪裡來？","From bacteria, such as lactic acid bacteria":"來自細菌，例如乳酸菌","From hops":"來自啤酒花","From added lemon juice":"來自添加的檸檬汁","From roasted malt":"來自烘烤麥芽","Lactic bacteria, active in fermentation and maturation, add acidity.":"乳酸菌在發酵和熟成期間作用，增加酸度。","Hops give bitterness, roasted malt coffee and chocolate; no lemon is added.":"啤酒花帶來苦味，烘烤麥芽帶來咖啡和巧克力；不會添加檸檬。","Which description fits Berliner weisse?":"哪一項描述符合柏林白啤酒（Berliner weisse）？","Straw, hazy, moderately sour, light body, low alcohol":"稻草色，混濁，適度的酸，酒體輕，酒精低","Gold, very sour, high alcohol, spontaneous fermentation":"金色，非常酸，酒精高，自然發酵","Black and roasted":"黑色、烘烤","Amber and very bitter":"琥珀色、非常苦","It is a light, moderately sour wheat beer with low or no bitterness.":"它是清淡、適度酸的小麥啤酒，苦味低或沒有苦味。","The second option is closer to geuze. Berliner weisse is neither dark nor bitter.":"第二個選項比較接近貴茲。柏林白啤酒既不是深色也不苦。","Which syrups is Berliner weisse sometimes served with?":"柏林白啤酒有時會搭配哪些糖漿飲用？","Raspberry or woodruff":"覆盆子或香車葉草","Mint or lemon":"薄荷或檸檬","Caramel or vanilla":"焦糖或香草","Cola or ginger":"可樂或薑","Raspberry or woodruff, a slightly bitter herb reminiscent of sweet hay.":"覆盆子或香車葉草，一種微苦、讓人想到甜乾草的香草。","The other options are not the traditional ones for this style.":"其他選項都不是這個風格的傳統搭配。","How is Berliner weisse typically made?":"柏林白啤酒通常怎麼釀造？","With cultured yeast and bacteria":"使用培養的酵母和細菌","By spontaneous fermentation":"以自然發酵","Without yeast":"不用酵母","With lager yeast only":"只用拉格酵母","Berliner weisse uses cultured yeast and bacteria.":"柏林白啤酒使用培養的酵母和細菌。","Spontaneous fermentation is geuze's method. Without yeast there is no alcohol, and lager yeast alone gives no sourness.":"自然發酵是貴茲的方法。沒有酵母就沒有酒精，而只用拉格酵母不會產生酸味。","Which sour style is made by spontaneous fermentation?":"哪種酸啤酒風格是自然發酵的？","Geuze comes from ambient yeast and bacteria, including Brett and lactic bacteria.":"貴茲（Geuze）來自環境中的酵母和細菌，包括 Brett 和乳酸菌。","Berliner weisse uses cultured microbes; saison and witbier are yeast-driven styles.":"柏林白啤酒使用培養的微生物；賽森和比利時白啤酒是酵母主導的風格。","Which aromas are typical of geuze?":"哪些香氣是貴茲的典型？","Farmyard (earth, hay) and fruit such as grapefruit, apple, apricot, rhubarb":"農舍（泥土、乾草）以及葡萄柚、蘋果、杏桃、大黃等水果","Caramel and raisin":"焦糖和葡萄乾","Geuze is complex: farmyard notes and lots of fruit, with a hint of bread crumb.":"貴茲很複雜：農舍調性和大量果香，帶一絲麵包心。","Coffee and chocolate suggest stout, banana and clove weissbier, caramel and raisin malty beers such as barley wine.":"咖啡和巧克力讓人想到司陶特，香蕉和丁香是德式小麥啤酒，焦糖和葡萄乾則是大麥酒等麥芽濃郁的啤酒。","Which statement about geuze is correct?":"關於貴茲，哪一項敘述正確？","It is sour, gold, with low or no bitterness and highly carbonated":"它是酸的、金色，苦味低或沒有，碳酸感高","It is black and very bitter":"它是黑色而且非常苦","It is a lager":"它是拉格","It has very low alcohol, under 2%":"它的酒精非常低，低於 2%","Geuze: gold, sour, low or no bitterness, medium-high alcohol, sediment and lots of bubbles.":"貴茲：金色、酸、苦味低或沒有、酒精中高、有沉澱和大量氣泡。","It is not black or bitter, not a lager, and its alcohol is medium to high.":"它不是黑色也不苦，不是拉格，酒精為中等到高。","What are the three main enemies of beer in storage?":"保存啤酒的三大敵人是什麼？","Oxygen, heat and light":"氧氣、熱和光","Cold, darkness and humidity":"寒冷、黑暗和濕氣","Carbon dioxide, cold and glass":"二氧化碳、寒冷和玻璃","Sugar, yeast and hops":"糖、酵母和啤酒花","Oxygen, heat and light easily damage beer.":"氧氣、熱和光很容易損害啤酒。","Cold and darkness protect it; keg CO2 shields it from oxygen.":"寒冷和黑暗能保護啤酒；桶中的 CO2 能讓它免於接觸氧氣。","What usually happens to a beer kept too long?":"啤酒放太久通常會怎麼樣？","Hop aroma and bitterness fade; paper or cardboard notes appear":"啤酒花香氣和苦味消退；出現紙或紙板味","It becomes more bitter and hoppy":"變得更苦、啤酒花味更重","It becomes stronger in alcohol":"酒精變得更高","It gains more bubbles":"氣泡變得更多","This is staling: hops and bitterness fade, cardboard notes arrive.":"這就是老化（staling）：啤酒花和苦味消退，出現紙板味。","Over time bitterness falls rather than rises; alcohol does not increase and bubbles tend to drop.":"隨著時間，苦味只會下降不會上升；酒精不會增加，氣泡也會減少。","Which container protects beer LEAST from light?":"哪種容器「最不能」保護啤酒免受光害？","Clear glass bottle":"透明玻璃瓶","Brown bottle":"棕色瓶","Can":"罐","Keg":"桶","Clear (or green) glass gives little or no protection: keep it in sealed boxes.":"透明（或綠色）玻璃幾乎沒有保護作用：要放在密封的箱子裡。","Cans and kegs are opaque; brown glass blocks almost all damaging light.":"罐和桶不透光；棕色玻璃能擋住幾乎所有有害的光線。","Why does keg beer stay fresh longer?":"為什麼桶裝啤酒能保持新鮮較久？","It is packed with carbon dioxide, which protects it from oxygen":"它充填了二氧化碳，能保護它免於接觸氧氣","It contains preservatives":"它含有防腐劑","It has more alcohol":"它的酒精較高","It is pasteurised twice":"它經過兩次加熱殺菌","The keg is packed with CO2, which keeps oxygen away.":"酒桶充填了 CO2，能隔絕氧氣。","The other reasons are not the point: protection from oxygen makes the difference.":"其他理由都不是重點：隔絕氧氣才是關鍵。","A bottle of beer has been opened: when should it be drunk?":"一瓶啤酒已經開瓶：應該什麼時候喝？","Straight away":"馬上喝","Within a week in the fridge":"放冰箱一週內喝","Within a month":"一個月內喝","Whenever, if recapped":"隨時都可以，只要重新蓋上","Once opened, bottles and cans should be drunk at once to keep aroma and carbonation.":"瓶裝和罐裝啤酒開了以後應該馬上喝，才能保有香氣和碳酸感。","Beer is unlike sake or wine: opened, it quickly loses bubbles and freshness.":"啤酒和清酒或葡萄酒不同：開了以後很快就會失去氣泡和新鮮感。","What causes light strike (skunking)?":"光害（臭鼬味）是什麼造成的？","Light acting on hop compounds":"光線作用在啤酒花成分上","Bacteria in beer lines":"啤酒管線中的細菌","Too much roasted malt":"太多烘烤麥芽","Excessive cold":"過度寒冷","Light changes hop compounds and creates unpleasant smells.":"光線改變啤酒花成分，產生難聞的氣味。","Bacteria in lines give vinegar and rancid butter. Roasted malt and cold do not cause this fault.":"管線中的細菌會帶來醋和腐敗奶油味。烘烤麥芽和寒冷都不會造成這種缺陷。","Which smells indicate light strike?":"哪些氣味代表光害？","Skunky, scorched hair, cat urine":"臭鼬味、燒焦頭髮味、貓尿味","Paper and wet cardboard":"紙和濕紙板","Caramel and toffee":"焦糖和太妃糖","Light strike gives a skunky, scorched-hair or cat-urine smell.":"光害會帶來臭鼬味、燒焦頭髮味或貓尿味。","Paper and cardboard signal staling; vinegar and rancid butter bacterial infection.":"紙和紙板代表老化；醋和腐敗奶油代表細菌感染。","A draught beer tastes of vinegar and rancid butter. What is the most likely cause?":"一款生啤酒嘗起來有醋和腐敗奶油味。最可能的原因是什麼？","Bacterial infection in poorly maintained beer lines":"維護不良的啤酒管線中有細菌感染","Light strike":"光害","A glass that is too cold":"杯子太冰","Too much hops":"啤酒花太多","Bacteria in the hoses connecting keg and tap give vinegar and rancid butter.":"連接酒桶和酒頭的管線中的細菌會帶來醋和腐敗奶油味。","Light strike smells different (skunky) and kegs are opaque. Cold and hops do not create vinegar.":"光害的氣味不同（臭鼬味），而且酒桶不透光。寒冷和啤酒花不會產生醋味。","What speeds up staling?":"什麼會加速老化？","Heat and oxygen":"熱和氧氣","Cold and darkness":"寒冷和黑暗","Brown bottles":"棕色瓶","Staling comes faster with heat and oxygen.":"熱和氧氣會讓老化來得更快。","Cold, dark, brown glass and CO2 protect beer rather than ageing it.":"寒冷、黑暗、棕色玻璃和 CO2 會保護啤酒，而不是讓它老化。","After pouring, bubbles cling to the sides of the glass. What does this show?":"倒酒後，氣泡附著在杯壁上。這代表什麼？","The glass is not completely clean":"杯子沒有完全洗乾淨","The beer is very fresh":"啤酒非常新鮮","The beer is bottle-conditioned":"啤酒經過瓶中二次發酵","The glass is too narrow":"杯子太窄","Clinging bubbles signal residue or dirt on the glass.":"附著的氣泡代表杯子上有殘留物或髒污。","They do not depend on freshness, bottle-conditioning or glass shape.":"它們與新鮮度、瓶中二次發酵或杯型無關。","Which glass feature helps head retention?":"杯子的哪個特點有助於泡沫持久？","A narrow shape":"窄的形狀","A very wide, open bowl":"非常寬、開口大的杯身","A warm glass":"溫的杯子","Detergent residue":"清潔劑殘留","Narrow glasses help the foam last.":"窄的杯子有助於泡沫持久。","A rounded bowl helps swirling, inward walls hold aromas. Detergent harms the foam.":"圓弧的杯身方便搖杯，向內收的杯壁能留住香氣。清潔劑會破壞泡沫。","Pouring from the keg, how far do you fill with the glass tilted at 45°?":"從酒桶倒酒時，杯子傾斜 45° 要倒到多滿？","To about 70% full":"約七分滿（70%）","Right to the brim":"一直倒到杯緣","To 20%":"倒到 20%","The glass is never tilted":"杯子從不傾斜","Pour down the side to about 70%, then upright and pour into the centre for foam.":"沿著杯壁倒到約 70%，然後把杯子立直，往中央倒以形成泡沫。","Filling entirely tilted would leave little foam; 20% is too early.":"全程傾斜倒滿會讓泡沫很少；20% 太早了。","Which rule applies to the tap when pouring keg beer?":"從酒桶倒啤酒時，酒頭有什麼規則？","It must not touch the beer or the glass":"不能碰到啤酒或杯子","It should be dipped in the beer":"應該浸在啤酒裡","It is opened only halfway":"只開一半","It should rest on the glass rim":"應該靠在杯緣上","The tap never touches beer or glass, for hygiene; it is opened fully.":"基於衛生，酒頭絕不碰到啤酒或杯子；要完全打開。","The tap is opened fully, not halfway, and is never dipped or rested on the glass.":"酒頭要完全打開，不是開一半，也絕不浸入啤酒或靠在杯子上。","How is a crown-capped bottle opened correctly?":"皇冠蓋的瓶子怎麼正確打開？","Steady the bottle with one hand; remove the cap with the opener in one motion":"一手穩住瓶子；用開瓶器一個動作把瓶蓋取下","With several small taps":"輕敲好幾下","By shaking the bottle first":"先搖一搖瓶子","With a corkscrew":"用軟木塞開瓶器","One single, smooth motion while steadying the bottle.":"穩住瓶子，以單一順暢的動作打開。","Tapping or shaking makes the beer foam over; a corkscrew is for corks.":"敲打或搖晃會讓啤酒噴出泡沫；軟木塞開瓶器是用來開軟木塞的。","A bottle-conditioned beer with sediment is being served. What do you do?":"要侍酒一款有沉澱的瓶中二次發酵啤酒。你會怎麼做？","Pour carefully and stop when the sediment reaches the neck":"小心倒酒，沉澱到瓶頸時停止","Shake the bottle and pour everything":"搖一搖瓶子，全部倒出來","Filter the beer through a napkin":"用餐巾過濾啤酒","Throw away the first third":"倒掉前三分之一","Keep the bottle tilted and stop as the sediment nears the neck; a little beer stays behind.":"保持瓶子傾斜，沉澱接近瓶頸時停止；會有一點啤酒留在瓶中。","Rolling and pouring everything is for weissbier and witbier, not beers meant to stay clear.":"滾動瓶子並全部倒出是德式小麥啤酒和比利時白啤酒的做法，不適用於應該保持清澈的啤酒。","Why leave the bottle on the table after serving a beer with sediment?":"侍酒有沉澱的啤酒後，為什麼要把瓶子留在桌上？","So the drinker can choose to add the sediment":"讓飲用者自己選擇是否加入沉澱","To show the price":"為了展示價格","Because throwing it away is banned":"因為禁止丟掉","To let it cool":"為了讓它冷卻","The drinker decides whether to have the sediment in the glass.":"由飲用者決定杯中要不要有沉澱。","It is about personal choice: the other reasons make no sense.":"這是個人選擇的問題：其他理由都說不通。","How are bottled weissbier and witbier usually served?":"瓶裝的德式小麥啤酒和比利時白啤酒通常怎麼侍酒？","Gently roll the bottle before opening and pour everything":"開瓶前輕輕滾動瓶子，全部倒出","Leave the sediment in the bottle":"把沉澱留在瓶中","Filter them":"過濾它們","Serve them warm":"溫熱飲用","They are naturally hazy: the sediment is mixed back in.":"它們本來就是混濁的：沉澱會被混回酒中。","For these styles the sediment is not left behind; weissbier is served well chilled.":"這些風格不會把沉澱留下；德式小麥啤酒要充分冰鎮飲用。","At what temperature is a pilsner or weissbier served?":"皮爾森或德式小麥啤酒的侍酒溫度是多少？","Well chilled, 3–7 °C":"充分冰鎮，3–7 °C","Chilled, 7–12 °C":"冰涼，7–12 °C","Lightly chilled, 12–15 °C":"微涼，12–15 °C","Room temperature, 20 °C":"室溫，20 °C","Light-medium aroma and low-medium alcohol: well chilled, 3–7 °C.":"香氣淡到中等、酒精低到中等：充分冰鎮，3–7 °C。","7–12 °C suits porter and IPA, 12–15 °C barley wine and dubbel.":"7–12 °C 適合波特和 IPA，12–15 °C 適合大麥酒和比利時雙料。","At what temperature should a barley wine be served?":"大麥酒應該在什麼溫度侍酒？","Below freezing":"冰點以下","Complex, high-alcohol styles: 12–15 °C to enjoy their aromas.":"複雜、高酒精的風格：12–15 °C，才能享受它們的香氣。","Too cold would mute the barley wine's complex aromas.":"太冰會讓大麥酒複雜的香氣變得封閉。","Porter, American pale ale and American IPA are usually served…":"波特、美式淡色艾爾和美式 IPA 通常在什麼溫度侍酒？","chilled, 7–12 °C":"冰涼，7–12 °C","well chilled, 3–7 °C":"充分冰鎮，3–7 °C","lightly chilled, 12–15 °C":"微涼，12–15 °C","warm, 40 °C":"溫熱，40 °C","Medium to pronounced aroma, medium to high alcohol: 7–12 °C.":"香氣中等到明顯、酒精中等到高：7–12 °C。","3–7 °C is for lagers and weissbier, 12–15 °C for barley wine and dubbel.":"3–7 °C 適合拉格和德式小麥啤酒，12–15 °C 適合大麥酒和比利時雙料。","What effect do salt and acidity in food have on beer?":"食物中的鹹味和酸味對啤酒有什麼影響？","Sweeter, less acidic, less bitter":"更甜、較不酸、較不苦","Less sweet, more acidic, more bitter":"較不甜、更酸、更苦","Salt and acidity soften the beer.":"鹹味和酸味會讓啤酒變得柔和。","Less sweet, more acidic and more bitter is the effect of sweetness and umami. Chilli raises perceived alcohol.":"較不甜、更酸、更苦是甜味和鮮味的影響。辣椒會提高感受到的酒精。","How does a very sweet dessert change the perception of beer?":"非常甜的甜點如何改變對啤酒的感受？","Less sweet, more acidic and more bitter":"較不甜、更酸、更苦","Sweeter and less bitter":"更甜、較不苦","More fizzy":"氣泡感更強","Sweetness in food lowers beer's sweetness and raises its acidity and bitterness.":"食物的甜味會降低啤酒的甜度，提高它的酸度和苦味。","The 'sweeter, less bitter' effect comes from salt and acidity.":"「更甜、較不苦」的效果來自鹹味和酸味。","What does chilli heat do to a beer?":"辣椒的辣度對啤酒有什麼影響？","Increases the perception of alcohol":"增加對酒精的感受","Makes it sweeter":"讓它更甜","Chilli heat accentuates the sense of alcohol, especially in strong beers.":"辣椒的辣度會突顯酒精感，尤其是烈的啤酒。","Chilli neither sweetens the beer nor removes bitterness.":"辣椒既不會讓啤酒變甜，也不會去除苦味。","A very spicy dish: which beer is most likely to burn?":"一道非常辣的菜：哪種啤酒最可能帶來灼熱感？","A tripel or a barley wine":"比利時三料或大麥酒","A Berliner weisse":"柏林白啤酒","A light pale lager":"清淡的淡色拉格","A blonde ale":"金色艾爾","High or very high-alcohol styles greatly increase the chilli burn.":"酒精高或非常高的風格會大幅增加辣椒的灼熱感。","Berliner weisse, light lagers and blonde ales have low or medium alcohol.":"柏林白啤酒、清淡的拉格和金色艾爾酒精低或中等。","With an umami-rich dish, which style may seem even more bitter?":"搭配富含鮮味的菜餚時，哪種風格可能顯得更苦？","High-bitterness styles like American IPA get even more bitter with umami, sweetness or bitterness.":"美式 IPA 這類高苦味風格，遇到鮮味、甜味或苦味會變得更苦。","Weissbier and Berliner weisse have low bitterness; helles low to medium.":"德式小麥啤酒和柏林白啤酒苦味低；慕尼黑淡色拉格苦味低到中等。","Why can a geuze become difficult with a dessert?":"為什麼貴茲搭配甜點可能會變得難搭？","Sweetness in the food makes it seem even more acidic":"食物的甜味讓它顯得更酸","Sweetness makes it seem stronger":"甜味讓它顯得更烈","The dessert makes it cloudy":"甜點讓它變混濁","The dessert removes the bubbles":"甜點讓氣泡消失","High-acidity styles seem even more acidic with sweetness or umami in food.":"高酸度的風格遇到食物中的甜味或鮮味會顯得更酸。","Dessert does not affect alcohol, clarity or bubbles.":"甜點不會影響酒精、清澈度或氣泡。","Why should beer and dish have a similar flavour intensity?":"為什麼啤酒和菜餚的風味強度應該相近？","So one does not overpower the other":"才不會一方壓過另一方","So the beer is colder":"讓啤酒更冰","To increase the alcohol":"為了增加酒精","To reduce the bubbles":"為了減少氣泡","With different intensities, the stronger one masks the more delicate.":"強度不同時，較強的一方會掩蓋較細緻的一方。","Intensity has nothing to do with temperature, alcohol or bubbles.":"強度與溫度、酒精或氣泡無關。","A stout with coffee and chocolate notes alongside a cocoa dessert: which principle does this pairing use?":"帶有咖啡和巧克力調性的司陶特搭配可可甜點：這個搭配運用了哪個原則？","Similar or complementary aromas in beer and food":"啤酒和食物有相似或互補的香氣","Salt reduces bitterness":"鹽能降低苦味","Chilli raises alcohol":"辣椒會提高酒精感","Colour contrast":"顏色對比","Similar aromas create a familiar connection between beer and dish.":"相似的香氣在啤酒和菜餚之間建立熟悉的連結。","No salt or chilli is involved here, and colour is not a pairing criterion.":"這裡沒有用到鹽或辣椒，而顏色不是搭配的標準。","Why can the same pairing please one person and not another?":"為什麼同樣的搭配，有人喜歡、有人不喜歡？","People have different preferences and sensitivities":"每個人的喜好和敏感度不同","Because the beer changes from glass to glass":"因為每一杯啤酒都不一樣","Because there are fixed rules":"因為有固定的規則","It never happens":"這種事從不發生","People perceive tastes and aromas differently: interactions are principles, not rules.":"每個人對味道和香氣的感受不同：交互作用是原則，不是規則。","Precisely because there are no fixed rules, the individual matters.":"正因為沒有固定的規則，個人才是關鍵。","Beer is a hugely varied category, from clear golden pilsners to opaque black stouts. Yet they all share something: every beer is an alcoholic drink obtained by fermentation, normally from malt (malted grains), water and yeast, with hops for flavouring.":"啤酒是非常多樣的類別，從清澈的金色皮爾森到不透明的黑色司陶特都有。但它們都有一個共同點：每一款啤酒都是發酵而成的酒精飲料，通常以麥芽（製成麥芽的穀物）、水和酵母釀造，並以啤酒花調味。","To make alcohol you need a sugary liquid. Yeast is added; it eats the sugar and turns it into alcohol, producing carbon dioxide (CO2) and aromas at the same time: this is fermentation. Alcohol is measured as alcohol by volume: 5% abv means 5% of the liquid is alcohol. For beer, a handy scale is: low up to 4%, medium 4.1–5.9%, high 6–9%, very high above 9%.":"要產生酒精，需要含糖的液體。加入酵母後，它吃掉糖並把糖變成酒精，同時產生二氧化碳（CO2）和香氣：這就是發酵。酒精以酒精體積百分比表示：5% abv 代表液體中有 5% 是酒精。對啤酒來說，一個好用的分級是：低為 4% 以下，中等 4.1–5.9%，高 6–9%，非常高為 9% 以上。","Beer: fermented alcoholic drink from malt, water and yeast, flavoured with hops":"啤酒：以麥芽、水和酵母發酵而成的酒精飲料，以啤酒花調味","Fermentation: sugar + yeast → alcohol + CO2 + aromas":"發酵：糖 + 酵母 → 酒精 + CO2 + 香氣","Alcohol: low ≤4% · medium 4.1–5.9% · high 6–9% · very high >9%":"酒精：低 ≤4% · 中等 4.1–5.9% · 高 6–9% · 非常高 >9%","Four ingredients and one conversion":"四種原料和一次轉化","Malt supplies the sugar that yeast will turn into alcohol, gives most of the colour and can bring many aromas. Water is, by volume, the main ingredient: it is the liquid in which the yeast works, and breweries use a lot of it, so they need a plentiful, reliable supply. Hops (the cones of the plant) were first used mainly for their antibacterial, preserving effect; today they are prized for bitterness and aroma. Yeast creates the alcohol and carbonation and can add aromas.":"麥芽提供酵母要轉化成酒精的糖，帶來大部分的顏色，也能帶來許多香氣。以體積來說，水是最主要的原料：它是酵母工作的液體，酒廠用量很大，所以需要充足、可靠的水源。啤酒花（植株的毬花）最初主要因為抗菌、保存的效果而使用；如今則因苦味和香氣而受重視。酵母產生酒精和碳酸，也能增加香氣。","Malt, however, reaches the brewery with no sugar: the grains are full of starch, sugars bonded into long chains that yeast cannot eat. Enzymes are needed: catalysts that speed up reactions and break starch into shorter sugars. This is starch conversion. Conveniently, malt supplies both the starch and the enzymes: when milled malt meets hot water, the enzymes turn the starch into sugar, which dissolves into a sugary liquid.":"不過，麥芽送到酒廠時並不含糖：穀粒裡滿是澱粉，也就是連結成長鏈、酵母無法吃的糖。需要酵素：一種能加速反應、把澱粉切成較短糖分子的催化劑。這就是澱粉轉化。方便的是，麥芽同時提供澱粉和酵素：碾碎的麥芽遇到熱水時，酵素把澱粉變成糖，糖溶解成含糖的液體。","Malt: sugar, colour, aromas":"麥芽：糖、顏色、香氣","Water: the main ingredient by volume":"水：以體積計最主要的原料","Hops: once a preservative, now bitterness and aroma":"啤酒花：過去用於保存，現在帶來苦味和香氣","Malt brings starch and enzymes: with hot water starch becomes sugar":"麥芽提供澱粉和酵素：加入熱水後澱粉變成糖","The life of a grain, and malting":"穀物的一生與製麥","For brewers the most important grain is barley, but wheat, maize (corn), oats, rye, rice and sorghum are used too. A grain is made of an embryo (the future plant), an energy store in the form of starch, and a protective casing, the husk. When spring brings enough warmth and moisture, the embryo wakes up and, to feed itself, releases enzymes that turn the starch into sugars.":"對釀酒師來說，最重要的穀物是大麥，但小麥、玉米、燕麥、黑麥、米和高粱也會使用。穀粒由胚芽（未來的植株）、以澱粉形式儲存的能量，以及保護外殼（穀殼）構成。春天帶來足夠的溫暖和濕氣時，胚芽甦醒，為了養活自己而釋放酵素，把澱粉變成糖。","Malting mimics that spring. 1. Steeping: the grains are submerged in water. 2. Germination: once they have absorbed enough water, the embryo grows and enzymes form inside the grain. 3. Kilning: growth must be stopped, or the embryo would use up the starch; the grains are heated and dried with warm air in a kiln. The dry malt, holding starch and enzymes, keeps until the brewer needs it, and kilning also creates colour and aromas.":"製麥就是模擬那個春天。1. 浸麥：把穀物浸在水中。2. 發芽：吸收足夠的水分後，胚芽生長，穀粒內部形成酵素。3. 烘麥：生長必須停止，否則胚芽會把澱粉用光；穀物在烘麥窯中以溫暖的空氣加熱乾燥。含有澱粉和酵素的乾燥麥芽可以保存到釀酒師需要時，而烘麥也會創造顏色和香氣。","Barley first; also wheat, maize, oats, rye, rice, sorghum":"大麥最重要；也有小麥、玉米、燕麥、黑麥、米、高粱","Grain: embryo, starch (energy store), husk":"穀粒：胚芽、澱粉（能量儲存）、穀殼","Malting: steeping → germination (enzymes) → kilning":"製麥：浸麥 → 發芽（酵素）→ 烘麥","Kilning stops growth and creates colour and aromas":"烘麥停止生長，並創造顏色和香氣","Base malts and speciality malts":"基礎麥芽和特殊麥芽","Varying the temperature and length of kilning gives different malts; some are roasted too. Base malts make up most of the malt a brewer uses: they are kilned at the lowest temperatures, so their enzymes survive to work later during mashing. They give aromas of water cracker, bread dough, bread crumb and light honey and, used alone, a straw or gold beer.":"改變烘麥的溫度和時間，就能得到不同的麥芽；有些還會再烘烤。基礎麥芽占釀酒師所用麥芽的大部分：它們以最低的溫度烘麥，所以酵素得以保留，之後在糖化時發揮作用。它們帶來蘇打餅乾、麵團、麵包心和淡淡蜂蜜的香氣，單獨使用時會得到稻草色或金色的啤酒。","Speciality malts are used for colour and aroma, usually in small amounts alongside base malts. They are made by kilning hotter or longer, or by roasting malt at even higher temperatures, which damages or destroys their enzymes. Possible aromas: digestive biscuit (graham cracker), bread crust, toast, toasted nuts, caramel, dried fruit, candy floss, coffee and chocolate. Colours: amber, copper, brown, even black.":"特殊麥芽用來增加顏色和香氣，通常少量搭配基礎麥芽使用。它們以更高溫或更長時間烘麥，或以更高的溫度烘烤麥芽而成，這會破壞或摧毀它們的酵素。可能的香氣：消化餅乾（全麥餅乾）、麵包皮、烤麵包、烤堅果、焦糖、果乾、棉花糖、咖啡和巧克力。顏色：琥珀色、銅色、棕色，甚至黑色。","Base malts: kilned lowest, enzymes intact, most of the recipe":"基礎麥芽：最低溫烘麥，酵素完好，占配方大部分","Base malts: water cracker, bread dough, crumb, light honey; straw or gold colour":"基礎麥芽：蘇打餅乾、麵團、麵包心、淡淡的蜂蜜；稻草色或金色","Speciality malts: more heat or roasting, enzymes damaged, small amounts":"特殊麥芽：更高溫或烘烤，酵素受損，少量使用","Speciality: biscuit, toast, caramel, dried fruit, coffee, chocolate; amber to black":"特殊麥芽：餅乾、烤麵包、焦糖、果乾、咖啡、巧克力；琥珀色到黑色","Other sugar sources and the grain bill":"其他糖源與穀物配方","Other grains, sugars or syrups are sometimes used alongside malt: they provide fermentable sugar and can change texture and aroma. Rice and maize, like most sugars and syrups, tend to give lighter aroma intensity and lighter body. Wheat, on the other hand, can give a smooth, creamy texture and add to haziness.":"有時會搭配麥芽使用其他穀物、糖或糖漿：它們提供可發酵的糖，也能改變口感和香氣。米和玉米，以及大多數糖和糖漿，通常讓香氣強度和酒體變輕。小麥則能帶來滑順綿密的口感，並增加混濁度。","The grain bill is a beer's cereal recipe: which malts and grains go in, and how much of each. It can be a single malt, but most recipes use a mix: a base malt makes up the majority, bringing starch and plenty of enzymes for conversion, while small amounts of speciality malts set the colour, aromas and complexity.":"穀物配方（grain bill）是一款啤酒的穀物配方：用哪些麥芽和穀物，各用多少。它可以只用一種麥芽，但大多數配方使用混合：基礎麥芽占大部分，提供澱粉和充足的轉化酵素，少量的特殊麥芽則決定顏色、香氣和複雜度。","Rice, maize, sugars, syrups: lighter aroma intensity and body":"米、玉米、糖、糖漿：香氣強度和酒體較輕","Wheat: smooth, creamy texture and haze":"小麥：滑順綿密的口感和混濁","Grain bill: mostly base malt + a little speciality malt":"穀物配方：主要是基礎麥芽 + 少量特殊麥芽","Milling and mashing":"碾磨和糖化","Production follows six key stages: milling, mashing, wort boiling, fermentation, carbonation and packaging. It starts by milling (crushing) the malted grains: the milled grain is called grist and moves straight on to the next stage.":"生產分為六個關鍵階段：碾磨、糖化、麥汁煮沸、發酵、充氣和包裝。先把製好的麥芽碾磨（壓碎）：碾磨後的穀物稱為碎麥芽（grist），直接進入下一個階段。","Mashing begins when the grist is mixed with hot water, making the mash. The malt enzymes turn the starch into sugars, which dissolve into a sugary liquid still mixed with solid bits, mainly husks. At the end the liquid is separated from the solids: the liquid is called wort and the leftover solids are spent grains.":"碎麥芽與熱水混合時，糖化就開始了，形成糖化醪。麥芽的酵素把澱粉變成糖，糖溶解成含糖的液體，但仍混有固體碎屑，主要是穀殼。最後把液體和固體分離：液體稱為麥汁，剩下的固體是麥渣。","Six stages: milling, mashing, boiling, fermentation, carbonation, packaging":"六個階段：碾磨、糖化、煮沸、發酵、充氣、包裝","Milled malt = grist":"碾磨過的麥芽 = 碎麥芽","Grist + hot water = mash; enzymes turn starch to sugar":"碎麥芽 + 熱水 = 糖化醪；酵素把澱粉變成糖","Separated liquid = wort; solids = spent grains":"分離出的液體 = 麥汁；固體 = 麥渣","Boiling, cooling, fermenting":"煮沸、冷卻、發酵","The wort is then boiled. Boiling kills microorganisms, prevents spoilage and helps make the beer safe to drink; it is also when the main hop additions are made. After boiling, the wort is cooled rapidly to a temperature suitable for fermentation.":"接著把麥汁煮沸。煮沸能殺死微生物、防止變質，讓啤酒可以安全飲用；這也是主要加入啤酒花的時候。煮沸後，麥汁會快速冷卻到適合發酵的溫度。","The cooled wort goes into a fermentation vessel where yeast is added. During fermentation the yeast eats the sugars and creates alcohol, carbon dioxide and aromas. Remember the order: mill → mash → boil (with hops) → cool → ferment (with yeast).":"冷卻的麥汁進入發酵槽，在那裡加入酵母。發酵時，酵母吃掉糖，產生酒精、二氧化碳和香氣。記住順序：碾磨 → 糖化 → 煮沸（加啤酒花）→ 冷卻 → 發酵（加酵母）。","Boiling: kills microorganisms, makes beer safe":"煮沸：殺死微生物，讓啤酒安全","Main hop additions happen during the boil":"主要的啤酒花在煮沸時加入","Rapid cooling, then yeast in the fermenter":"快速冷卻，然後在發酵槽加入酵母","Bubbles and packaging":"氣泡與包裝","When beer is carbonated, carbon dioxide dissolves in it under pressure: the bubbles rise in the glass, are felt in the mouth and build the foam. Yeast already makes some CO2 during fermentation; to top this up, carbon dioxide that was bought or recovered from earlier fermentations can be injected. Alternatively, a further fermentation can take place in the sealed bottle: this is bottle-conditioning, which leaves a yeast sediment at the bottom.":"啤酒充氣時，二氧化碳在加壓下溶入啤酒：氣泡在杯中上升，在口中感受得到，也形成泡沫。酵母在發酵時已經產生一些 CO2；為了補足，可以注入購買或從之前發酵中回收的二氧化碳。另一種方法是在密封的瓶中再次發酵：這就是瓶中二次發酵，會在瓶底留下酵母沉澱。","Finally, the beer must be packaged so it can be sold and distributed. The most widely used containers are cans, bottles and kegs.":"最後，啤酒必須包裝才能販售和配送。最常用的容器是罐、瓶和桶。","Carbonation: CO2 dissolved under pressure → bubbles and foam":"充氣：CO2 在加壓下溶解 → 氣泡和泡沫","CO2 from fermentation, topped up by injected CO2 (bought or recovered)":"CO2 來自發酵，再以注入的 CO2（購買或回收）補足","Bottle-conditioning: yeast sediment":"瓶中二次發酵：酵母沉澱","Packaging: cans, bottles, kegs":"包裝：罐、瓶、桶","The hop plant and its varieties":"啤酒花植株與品種","Hops are climbing plants. Each spring new shoots come up from the ground; the bines that grow from them produce hop cones over the year, the part brewers want. In autumn the bines are cut near the ground and the cones are harvested, then dried so they can be kept a long time without rotting. Dried cones can be used as they are, but that is relatively rare: far more often they are milled and pressed into space-saving pellets. Hops are packed and refrigerated to keep their bitterness and aroma.":"啤酒花是攀緣植物。每年春天，新芽從地面冒出；長出的藤蔓在一年中結出啤酒花毬花，也就是釀酒師需要的部分。秋天時，藤蔓在靠近地面處被割下，採收毬花，接著乾燥，才能長時間保存而不腐爛。乾燥的毬花可以直接使用，但比較少見：更常見的是碾碎並壓製成節省空間的顆粒。啤酒花會包裝並冷藏，以保持苦味和香氣。","There are hundreds of hop varieties, each with slightly different aromas, aroma intensity and bitterness, and each with a climate it grows best in. So the well-known hop countries are linked with hop styles. Traditional German, Czech or British hops are known for subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy or fruity aromas. American, New Zealand or Australian hops tend to show intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical fruit or pine notes. New varieties appear every year, though, so every hop country can produce a wide range of aromas.":"啤酒花品種有數百種，每一種的香氣、香氣強度和苦味都略有不同，也各有最適合生長的氣候。所以知名的啤酒花產國都和某種啤酒花風格連在一起。傳統德國、捷克或英國啤酒花以細微的辛香、花香、草本、泥土或果香聞名。美國、紐西蘭或澳洲啤酒花往往帶有強烈的柑橘、核果、熱帶水果或松木調性。不過每年都有新品種出現，所以每個啤酒花產國都能產出多樣的香氣。","The cone is the part used; dried, usually turned into pellets":"使用的部分是毬花；乾燥後，通常製成顆粒","Packed and refrigerated to keep bitterness and aroma":"包裝並冷藏，以保持苦味和香氣","German, Czech, British: subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy, fruity":"德國、捷克、英國：細微的辛香、花香、草本、泥土、果香","American, NZ, Australian: intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical, pine":"美國、紐西蘭、澳洲：強烈的柑橘、核果、熱帶水果、松木","When to add hops, and other flavourings":"何時加入啤酒花，以及其他調味材料","Hops go into the boiling wort to extract bitterness and aroma, and timing decides what they give. For bitterness they go in near the start of the boil, as bitterness needs heat and time. For aroma they go in near the end, because aromas escape if boiled too long. Hops can also be added later, during or after fermentation, at a lower temperature: this dry hopping adds aroma. Brewers may use one variety or a blend; some varieties are for bitterness, some for aroma, others for both.":"啤酒花加入沸騰的麥汁中，以萃取苦味和香氣，而加入的時機決定它帶來什麼。要苦味就在煮沸開始時加入，因為苦味需要熱度和時間。要香氣就在接近結束時加入，因為煮太久香氣會散失。啤酒花也可以更晚加入，在發酵期間或之後、較低的溫度下：這種乾投會增加香氣。釀酒師可以使用單一品種或混合；有些品種用於苦味，有些用於香氣，有些兩者皆可。","Hops are the most widely used flavouring, but not the only one. Before hops spread, herbs and spices gave aroma or bitterness, and some brewers still use them. Fruits such as cherries and raspberries, plus citrus peel and coriander seed, have long featured in certain traditional Belgian styles. In most countries there are no limits as long as the ingredient is edible and practical: more unusual choices include pumpkin, honey, chilli and coffee.":"啤酒花是最常用的調味材料，但不是唯一的。在啤酒花普及之前，是用香草和香料帶來香氣或苦味，有些釀酒師至今仍在使用。櫻桃、覆盆子等水果，以及柑橘皮和芫荽籽，長久以來都出現在某些傳統比利時風格中。在大多數國家，只要原料可食用且實際可行就沒有限制：比較特別的選擇包括南瓜、蜂蜜、辣椒和咖啡。","Early in the boil → bitterness (needs heat and time)":"煮沸初期 → 苦味（需要熱度和時間）","Late in the boil → aroma (aromas escape)":"煮沸後段 → 香氣（香氣會散失）","Dry hopping: during or after fermentation, cooler, for aroma":"乾投：發酵期間或之後，溫度較低，增加香氣","Other flavourings: herbs, spices; fruit, citrus peel, coriander in Belgian styles":"其他調味材料：香草、香料；比利時風格中的水果、柑橘皮、芫荽","Ale yeast and lager yeast":"艾爾酵母和拉格酵母","Yeast's main job is to create alcohol, but it can also have a big effect on aroma. Brewing uses two main species, known as ale yeast and lager yeast: they behave differently and are behind one of the main divisions of beer styles, ales versus lagers.":"酵母的主要工作是產生酒精，但它對香氣也有很大的影響。釀造使用兩個主要的酵母種類，稱為艾爾酵母和拉格酵母：它們的表現不同，也造成啤酒風格的主要分類之一：艾爾與拉格。","Ale yeast works fast, likes fairly warm conditions and can create many different fruity and spicy aromas; there are many strains, each with its own signature, so strains are chosen to create particular styles. Beers made with ale yeast are ales. Lager yeast usually ferments more slowly and at a cooler temperature, has fewer strains and contributes less aroma. Beers made with lager yeast are lagers.":"艾爾酵母發酵快，喜歡相當溫暖的環境，能產生許多不同的果香和辛香；菌株很多，各有自己的特色，所以會選用特定菌株來創造特定風格。用艾爾酵母釀的啤酒是艾爾。拉格酵母通常發酵較慢、溫度較低，菌株較少，帶來的香氣也較少。用拉格酵母釀的啤酒是拉格。","Two main species: ale and lager → the ale/lager split":"兩個主要種類：艾爾和拉格 → 艾爾／拉格的劃分","Ale: quick, warmer, fruity and spicy aromas, many strains":"艾爾：快、較溫暖、果香和辛香、菌株多","Lager: slower, cooler, less aroma, fewer strains":"拉格：較慢、較涼、香氣較少、菌株較少","Brett, bacteria and spontaneous fermentation":"Brett、細菌與自然發酵","Besides the two main yeasts, other yeasts and even bacteria are used. Brettanomyces (Brett) adds complex aromas: fruity ones such as ripe pineapple and peach, and farmyard, leather, hay and earth. Lactic acid bacteria, the same kind used for yoghurt and kimchi, give beer acidity (sourness).":"除了兩種主要酵母，也會使用其他酵母，甚至細菌。酒香酵母（Brettanomyces，Brett）帶來複雜的香氣：熟鳳梨、桃子等果香，以及農舍、皮革、乾草和泥土。乳酸菌和用來做優格、泡菜的是同一類，會讓啤酒帶有酸度（酸味）。","Wild yeast lives everywhere, floating in the air and sitting on surfaces, yet almost every beer relies on cultured yeast, selected and grown in a lab: usually a single strain of ale or lager yeast, sometimes alongside cultured Brett or lactic acid bacteria. Some beers, however, are made by spontaneous fermentation: the brewer never adds cultured yeast or bacteria and relies on the ambient ones living in and around the brewery, so many different types grow in the wort.":"野生酵母無所不在，飄在空氣中、附著在物體表面，但幾乎每一款啤酒都依靠在實驗室中篩選並培養的培養酵母：通常是單一菌株的艾爾或拉格酵母，有時搭配培養的 Brett 或乳酸菌。不過，有些啤酒是自然發酵的：釀酒師完全不添加培養的酵母或細菌，而是依靠生活在酒廠內外的環境微生物，因此麥汁中會生長出許多不同的種類。","Brett: ripe pineapple, peach, farmyard, leather, hay, earth":"Brett：熟鳳梨、桃子、農舍、皮革、乾草、泥土","Lactic acid bacteria: sourness":"乳酸菌：酸味","Nearly all beers: cultured yeast (usually one strain)":"幾乎所有啤酒：培養酵母（通常是單一菌株）","Spontaneous fermentation: nothing cultured, only ambient yeast and bacteria":"自然發酵：不用任何培養的微生物，只用環境中的酵母和細菌","Getting ready and looking at the beer":"準備與觀察啤酒","Good tasting needs the same method for every beer. First: no distracting smells or noises; good lighting and a white background; a clean glass with a wide bowl narrowing at the top to concentrate aromas; a clean palate, free of garlic, toothpaste or coffee. The tasting grid splits tasting into three parts: appearance, nose and palate.":"好的品飲需要每一款啤酒都用相同的方法。首先：沒有干擾的氣味或噪音；良好的照明和白色背景；乾淨的杯子，杯身寬、向杯口收窄以集中香氣；口腔乾淨，沒有大蒜、牙膏或咖啡的味道。品飲表把品飲分成三部分：外觀、香氣和口感。","Appearance: for clarity, look through the glass towards the light (clear, hazy, opaque); for colour, hold the glass against a white background: straw, gold, amber, copper, brown, black. Also note the foam (the head): how big it is and how long it lasts.":"外觀：評估清澈度時，透過杯子朝光源看（清澈、混濁、不透明）；評估顏色時，把杯子放在白色背景前：稻草色、金色、琥珀色、銅色、棕色、黑色。也要記下泡沫（酒帽）：有多厚、能維持多久。","No smells or noise; good light, white background":"沒有氣味或噪音；光線良好、白色背景","Clean glass, wide bowl narrowing; clean palate":"乾淨的杯子，杯身寬、向上收窄；口腔乾淨","Clarity: clear – hazy – opaque":"清澈度：清澈 – 混濁 – 不透明","Colour: straw, gold, amber, copper, brown, black; foam":"顏色：稻草色、金色、琥珀色、銅色、棕色、黑色；泡沫","Nose, palate and where aromas come from":"香氣、口感，以及香氣的來源","Nose: first sniff with the glass held by the stem below your nose, then with your nose in the glass; swirl to release more aromas and sniff again with short sniffs or a longer one. Palate: take a sip, move it round your mouth, then swallow or spit. Aromas on the palate are often the same as on the nose; also judge intensity, carbonation, body, alcohol, bitterness, sweetness and acidity.":"香氣：先握著杯腳把杯子放在鼻子下方聞，再把鼻子伸進杯中聞；搖杯讓更多香氣釋放，再以短促或較長的方式聞一次。口感：喝一口，讓它在口中轉一圈，然後吞下或吐掉。口中的香氣常與鼻聞相同；還要判斷強度、碳酸感、酒體、酒精、苦味、甜度和酸度。","Aromas are grouped by source. From malt and grain: bread (bread dough, water cracker, crumb, crust, digestive biscuit, toasted or burnt bread), confectionery (honey, caramel, candy floss, treacle), dried fruit (raisin, prune, date, fig) and nut or roasted notes (toasted nut, chocolate, coffee, cocoa). From hops: floral, berries, apple and pear, citrus, stone fruit, tropical fruit, herbaceous (grass, hay) and herbal (mint, tea), plus pine, spice and earth. From yeast: fruit (banana, apple, citrus and more), spice (clove, peppercorn), farmyard and leather, and others such as bubblegum or nail varnish.":"香氣依來源分組。來自麥芽和穀物：麵包類（麵團、蘇打餅乾、麵包心、麵包皮、消化餅乾、烤麵包或烤焦的麵包）、甜點類（蜂蜜、焦糖、棉花糖、糖蜜）、果乾（葡萄乾、黑棗、椰棗、無花果），以及堅果或烘烤調性（烤堅果、巧克力、咖啡、可可）。來自啤酒花：花香、莓果、蘋果和西洋梨、柑橘、核果、熱帶水果、青草味（青草、乾草）和草本（薄荷、茶），還有松木、辛香和泥土。來自酵母：水果（香蕉、蘋果、柑橘等）、辛香（丁香、胡椒粒）、農舍和皮革，以及泡泡糖或去光水等其他香氣。","Nose: below the nose, in the glass, then swirl and sniff again":"香氣：鼻子下方、杯中，再搖杯重聞","Palate: intensity, carbonation, body, alcohol, bitterness, sweetness, acidity":"口感：強度、碳酸感、酒體、酒精、苦味、甜度、酸度","Malt: bread, honey, caramel, dried fruit, coffee, chocolate":"麥芽：麵包、蜂蜜、焦糖、果乾、咖啡、巧克力","Hops: floral, citrus, tropical, pine, herbal · Yeast: banana, clove, pepper, farmyard":"啤酒花：花香、柑橘、熱帶、松木、草本 · 酵母：香蕉、丁香、胡椒、農舍","A beer style is a set of characteristics, achieved with a certain mix of ingredients and techniques, linked to a name. The world's most popular beer is an easy-drinking pale lager, made everywhere. For these styles brewers use only base malts (lightly kilned malted barley): whether ale or lager, the colour is straw or gold and the aromas recall bread crumb, bread dough or water cracker. If sugar, syrup or neutral grains such as rice go into the recipe, the beer has lighter aroma intensity and body than an all-malt beer.":"啤酒風格是一組特徵，以特定的原料和技術組合達成，並與一個名稱相連。全世界最受歡迎的啤酒是一種易飲的淡色拉格，各地都有釀造。這類風格只使用基礎麥芽（輕度烘麥的大麥麥芽）：無論是艾爾還是拉格，顏色都是稻草色或金色，香氣讓人想到麵包心、麵團或蘇打餅乾。如果配方中加入糖、糖漿或米這類中性穀物，啤酒的香氣強度和酒體會比全麥芽啤酒更輕。","American or international pale lager: straw or gold, light aroma intensity (bread dough, water cracker, sometimes a little hop), low or medium bitterness, medium alcohol, high carbonation. Munich helles ('hell' is German for bright or pale): a lager, usually gold, with bread crumb or water cracker plus subtle spicy, herbal or floral hop notes; low to medium bitterness, medium alcohol. Blonde ale (sometimes 'golden ale'): an easy ale, straw to gold, with subtle bread crumb, low to medium alcohol, medium bitterness, maybe a touch of fruit from the yeast and subtle hops.":"美式或國際淡色拉格：稻草色或金色，香氣強度淡（麵團、蘇打餅乾，有時有一點啤酒花），苦味低或中等，酒精中等，碳酸感高。慕尼黑淡色拉格（Munich helles；「hell」是德文的明亮或淡色）：一種拉格，通常是金色，帶有麵包心或蘇打餅乾香，加上細微的辛香、草本或花香啤酒花調性；苦味低到中等，酒精中等。金色艾爾（Blonde ale，有時稱「golden ale」）：一種易飲的艾爾，稻草色到金色，帶有細微的麵包心香，酒精低到中等，苦味中等，可能有一點酵母帶來的果香和細微的啤酒花。","Base malts only: straw or gold; crumb, dough, cracker":"只用基礎麥芽：稻草色或金色；麵包心、麵團、餅乾","Rice, syrups, sugar → lighter aroma and body":"米、糖漿、糖 → 香氣和酒體較輕","International pale lager: light aroma, high carbonation":"國際淡色拉格：香氣淡，碳酸感高","Munich helles (gold lager) · blonde/golden ale (ale)":"慕尼黑淡色拉格（金色拉格）· 金色艾爾 blonde／golden ale（艾爾）","Munich dunkel and brown ale":"慕尼黑深色拉格與棕色艾爾","Adding small amounts of speciality malts to base malts brings aromas of biscuit, bread crust, toast, toasted nuts, caramel, dried fruit, coffee and chocolate, and amber, copper, brown or black colours. Munich dunkel ('dunkel' is German for dark) is a copper to brown lager with toasted bread, bread crust, toasted nut and sometimes caramel or chocolate, plus at times subtle spicy, herbal or floral hop notes; low to medium bitterness, medium alcohol.":"在基礎麥芽中加入少量特殊麥芽，會帶來餅乾、麵包皮、烤麵包、烤堅果、焦糖、果乾、咖啡和巧克力的香氣，以及琥珀色、銅色、棕色或黑色。慕尼黑深色拉格（Munich dunkel；「dunkel」是德文的深色）是銅色到棕色的拉格，帶有烤麵包、麵包皮、烤堅果，有時有焦糖或巧克力，偶爾還有細微的辛香、草本或花香啤酒花調性；苦味低到中等，酒精中等。","Brown ale is an amber to brown ale with toasted nut, toasted bread and sometimes chocolate or caramel, sometimes with fruity yeast aromas. Some versions have subtle fruity, earthy or herbal hops, others more intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical or pine notes. Bitterness and alcohol both range from low to high: it is a broad style.":"棕色艾爾是琥珀色到棕色的艾爾，帶有烤堅果、烤麵包，有時有巧克力或焦糖，有時伴隨酵母帶來的果香。有些版本啤酒花細微，帶果香、泥土或草本調性，有些則有更強烈的柑橘、核果、熱帶或松木調性。苦味和酒精都從低到高：這是範圍很廣的風格。","Small amounts of speciality malt: biscuit, toast, caramel, coffee, chocolate; amber to black":"少量特殊麥芽：餅乾、烤麵包、焦糖、咖啡、巧克力；琥珀色到黑色","Munich dunkel: copper-brown lager, toast, nut; low-medium bitterness":"慕尼黑深色拉格：銅色到棕色的拉格，烤麵包、堅果；苦味中低","Brown ale: amber-brown ale, toasted nut; bitterness and alcohol low to high":"棕色艾爾：琥珀色到棕色的艾爾，烤堅果；苦味和酒精從低到高","Porter, stout and barley wine":"波特、司陶特與大麥酒","Porters and stouts are two closely related families of ales. They are brown or black, with malt aromas such as coffee or chocolate and sometimes caramel. Some have subtle hops, others more intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical or pine notes; fruity yeast aromas sometimes show too. Bitterness is low to high and alcohol low to very high. Very high-alcohol versions with pronounced roasted aromas often have 'imperial' in their name.":"波特和司陶特是關係密切的兩個艾爾家族。它們是棕色或黑色，帶有咖啡或巧克力等麥芽香氣，有時有焦糖。有些啤酒花細微，有些則有更強烈的柑橘、核果、熱帶或松木調性；有時也會出現酵母帶來的果香。苦味從低到高，酒精從低到非常高。酒精非常高、烘烤香氣明顯的版本，名稱中常有「imperial」（帝國）。","Barley wine is an ale, often amber (though it can range from gold to brown), with intense malt aromas: toasted bread, caramel, digestive biscuit, dried fruit. It sometimes has fruity yeast notes. Expect a full body, clear sweetness and an alcohol level that is high or very high. Hops range from subtle earthy, floral, fruity notes to more prominent pine, citrus or tropical fruit, with low to high bitterness. Barley wines are often suitable for ageing.":"大麥酒是一種艾爾，常為琥珀色（但從金色到棕色都有），帶有濃烈的麥芽香氣：烤麵包、焦糖、消化餅乾、果乾。有時帶有酵母的果香調性。酒體飽滿、甜味明顯，酒精高或非常高。啤酒花從細微的泥土、花香、果香調性，到較明顯的松木、柑橘或熱帶水果都有，苦味從低到高。大麥酒常常適合陳放。","Porter and stout: brown or black ales, coffee and chocolate":"波特和司陶特：棕色或黑色的艾爾，咖啡和巧克力","'Imperial': very high-alcohol, strongly roasted versions":"「帝國」（imperial）：酒精非常高、烘烤感強烈的版本","Barley wine: often amber, intense malt, full body, sweet, high or very high alcohol":"大麥酒：常為琥珀色，麥芽香濃烈，酒體飽滿，甜，酒精高或非常高","Barley wine: often suitable for ageing":"大麥酒：常常適合陳放","Two ways to be hoppy; pilsner and bitter":"兩種表現啤酒花的方式；皮爾森與英式苦啤","Hops bring two things: bitterness and aroma. Some styles have medium or pronounced bitterness with restrained hop aroma: most hops go in early in the boil and few at the end, using traditional British, Czech or German hops (subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy or fruity). Others have high bitterness AND pronounced hop aroma: hops early (bitterness), later (flavour) and dry hopped (aroma), using American, New Zealand or Australian hops (citrus, stone fruit, tropical, pine). Recently some of these beers focus more on hop aroma than on bitterness, and many malt-driven styles now also appear in much hoppier versions.":"啤酒花帶來兩樣東西：苦味和香氣。有些風格苦味中等或明顯，但啤酒花香氣含蓄：大部分啤酒花在煮沸初期加入，最後只加少量，使用傳統英國、捷克或德國啤酒花（細微的辛香、花香、草本、泥土或果香）。另一些風格苦味高「而且」啤酒花香氣明顯：初期加入（苦味）、之後加入（風味）並乾投（香氣），使用美國、紐西蘭或澳洲啤酒花（柑橘、核果、熱帶、松木）。近年來有些這類啤酒更重視啤酒花香氣而不是苦味，許多麥芽主導的風格現在也出現了啤酒花更突出的版本。","Traditional Czech or German pilsner: a straw to gold lager with bread dough, light honey or bread crumb, and subtle spicy, floral or herbal hops; medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol. Bitter: a hop-driven ale from England, amber to copper, with toasted bread, bread crust, digestive biscuit or caramel, subtle fruity, earthy or herbal hops and sometimes fruity yeast notes; medium to high bitterness, alcohol low to high.":"傳統捷克或德國皮爾森：稻草色到金色的拉格，帶有麵團、淡淡的蜂蜜或麵包心，以及細微的辛香、花香或草本啤酒花；苦味中等到高，酒精中等。英式苦啤（Bitter）：來自英格蘭、啤酒花主導的艾爾，琥珀色到銅色，帶有烤麵包、麵包皮、消化餅乾或焦糖，細微的果香、泥土或草本啤酒花，有時有酵母的果香調性；苦味中等到高，酒精從低到高。","Bitterness with restrained aroma: hops mostly early, traditional European hops":"苦味明顯但香氣含蓄：啤酒花多在初期加入，傳統歐洲啤酒花","High bitterness and intense aroma: early, late and dry hops, New World hops":"高苦味和強烈香氣：初期、後段加入並乾投，新世界啤酒花","Czech or German pilsner: straw-gold lager, medium-high bitterness":"捷克或德國皮爾森：稻草色到金色的拉格，苦味中高","Bitter: English amber-copper ale, biscuit and caramel, medium-high bitterness":"英式苦啤：英國琥珀色到銅色的艾爾，餅乾和焦糖，苦味中高","American pale ale (APA): gold to amber, with hop aromas from citrus, stone and tropical fruit to pine, and subtle malt (bread crumb, sometimes toast or digestive biscuit); sometimes fruity yeast notes. Medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol. American IPA (India pale ale) can be seen as a stronger APA with even more bitterness and hop aroma: gold to amber, defined by high bitterness and pine, resin, citrus, tropical and stone fruit aromas, with subtle malt and medium to high alcohol.":"美式淡色艾爾（APA）：金色到琥珀色，啤酒花香氣從柑橘、核果、熱帶水果到松木，麥芽細微（麵包心，有時有烤麵包或消化餅乾）；有時有酵母的果香調性。苦味中等到高，酒精中等。美式 IPA（India pale ale，印度淡色艾爾）可以看作更烈的 APA，苦味和啤酒花香氣更強：金色到琥珀色，以高苦味和松木、樹脂、柑橘、熱帶水果、核果香氣為特徵，麥芽細微，酒精中等到高。","Hazy IPA (also New England IPA): straw to gold and distinctly hazy, with subtle malt (water cracker, bread crumb), stone fruit, tropical and citrus hop aromas and sometimes fruity yeast notes. It is typically LESS bitter than American IPA (low to medium bitterness), with medium to high alcohol: the example of beers focused on hop aroma rather than bitterness.":"霧濁 IPA（Hazy IPA，也稱新英格蘭 IPA）：稻草色到金色，明顯混濁，麥芽細微（蘇打餅乾、麵包心），帶有核果、熱帶和柑橘的啤酒花香氣，有時有酵母的果香調性。它通常比美式 IPA「苦味更低」（苦味低到中等），酒精中等到高：是重視啤酒花香氣而非苦味的啤酒代表。","APA: gold-amber, citrus-tropical-pine hops, medium-high bitterness, medium alcohol":"APA：金色到琥珀色，柑橘、熱帶、松木的啤酒花，苦味中高，酒精中等","American IPA: stronger APA, high bitterness, pine and resin, medium-high alcohol":"美式 IPA：更烈的 APA，苦味高，松木和樹脂，酒精中高","Hazy/New England IPA: hazy, straw-gold, very aromatic, LESS bitter":"霧濁／新英格蘭 IPA：混濁，稻草色到金色，非常香，苦味「較低」","Weissbier and witbier":"德式小麥啤酒與比利時白啤酒","In yeast-driven styles the yeast aromas are the signature. Since lagers have few yeast aromas, these are all ales: fruity (tropical, pome, citrus) and sometimes spicy (clove, peppercorn). Weissbier (also called hefeweizen) is typically straw to gold and cloudy/hazy: banana and clove from the yeast balance bread crumb from the wheat; low bitterness, medium alcohol, typically high carbonation. 'Weiss' is German for white and 'Weizen' for wheat: both words name German wheat beers.":"在酵母主導的風格中，酵母香氣就是招牌。因為拉格的酵母香氣很少，這些風格都是艾爾：帶果香（熱帶、仁果、柑橘），有時帶辛香（丁香、胡椒粒）。德式小麥啤酒（Weissbier，也稱 hefeweizen）通常是稻草色到金色，混濁：酵母帶來的香蕉和丁香，與小麥帶來的麵包心香氣取得平衡；苦味低，酒精中等，碳酸感通常很高。「Weiss」是德文的白色，「Weizen」是小麥：兩個詞都指德國的小麥啤酒。","Witbier is hazy and straw to gold, with subtle fruity and spicy yeast aromas, often complemented by citrus and floral notes from the coriander seed and orange peel used as flavourings. It has subtle bread crumb or light honey from the wheat and sometimes subtle spicy or herbal hops; low bitterness, medium alcohol. It may be labelled with the French term blanche, meaning 'white'.":"比利時白啤酒（Witbier）混濁，稻草色到金色，帶有細微的酵母果香和辛香，常搭配用作調味的芫荽籽和橙皮帶來的柑橘和花香調性。它有小麥帶來的細微麵包心或淡淡蜂蜜香，有時有細微的辛香或草本啤酒花；苦味低，酒精中等。酒標上可能寫著法文 blanche，意思是「白色」。","Yeast-driven styles: all ales; fruity and spicy yeast aromas":"酵母主導的風格：都是艾爾；酵母帶來果香和辛香","Weissbier/hefeweizen: hazy, banana and clove, wheat, low bitterness, high carbonation":"德式小麥啤酒／hefeweizen：混濁，香蕉和丁香，小麥，苦味低，碳酸感高","Weiss = white, Weizen = wheat":"Weiss = 白色，Weizen = 小麥","Witbier/blanche: hazy, coriander and orange peel, low bitterness":"比利時白啤酒／blanche：混濁，芫荽和橙皮，苦味低","Dubbel, tripel and saison":"比利時雙料、三料與賽森","Dubbel is copper to brown, with fruity apple, plum and prune and spicy clove or peppercorn from the yeast, balanced by toast, caramel or dried fruit from malt or caramelised sugars, and sometimes subtle hops. High alcohol, medium bitterness; bottle-conditioning usually leaves a sediment and a lively carbonation. Tripel is gold, with prominent fruity (orange, banana) and spicy (peppercorn, clove) yeast aromas and subtle light honey or bread crumb malt. Alcohol is high or very high, above that of a dubbel; medium bitterness; also bottle-conditioned with sediment and highly carbonated.":"比利時雙料（Dubbel）是銅色到棕色，帶有酵母帶來的蘋果、李子和黑棗果香，以及丁香或胡椒粒的辛香，與麥芽或焦糖化糖帶來的烤麵包、焦糖或果乾取得平衡，有時有細微的啤酒花。酒精高，苦味中等；瓶中二次發酵通常會留下沉澱和活潑的碳酸感。比利時三料（Tripel）是金色，酵母帶來的果香（柳橙、香蕉）和辛香（胡椒粒、丁香）很突出，麥芽細微，帶淡淡的蜂蜜或麵包心。酒精高或非常高，比雙料更高；苦味中等；同樣經瓶中二次發酵而有沉澱，碳酸感高。","Saison is most commonly gold to amber, with fruity and spicy yeast aromas (orange, peach, apple, a peppercorn note), bread crumb, toast or digestive biscuit from malt, and spicy, floral, fruity or earthy hops. It can be slightly sour. It is often bottle-conditioned, with sediment and lively bubbles; bitterness is typically medium and alcohol low to high.":"賽森（Saison）最常見的是金色到琥珀色，帶有酵母的果香和辛香（柳橙、桃子、蘋果、一絲胡椒粒），麥芽帶來的麵包心、烤麵包或消化餅乾，以及辛香、花香、果香或泥土的啤酒花香。它可能帶有輕微酸味。常經瓶中二次發酵，有沉澱和活潑的氣泡；苦味通常中等，酒精從低到高。","Dubbel: copper-brown, apple, plum, clove; high alcohol; sediment":"比利時雙料：銅色到棕色，蘋果、李子、丁香；酒精高；有沉澱","Tripel: gold, orange, banana, pepper; high or very high alcohol (above dubbel)":"比利時三料：金色，柳橙、香蕉、胡椒；酒精高或非常高（高於雙料）","Saison: gold-amber, orange, peach, pepper; can be slightly sour":"賽森：金色到琥珀色，柳橙、桃子、胡椒；可能帶輕微酸味","All three highly carbonated, often bottle-conditioned":"三者碳酸感都高，常經瓶中二次發酵","Where sourness comes from; Berliner weisse":"酸味從哪裡來；柏林白啤酒","In sour styles the sour character comes from bacteria, such as lactic acid bacteria, active during fermentation and maturation: they add acidity to the finished beer. Brettanomyces can also play a part, adding complex farmyard, hay, ripe pineapple and leather aromas.":"在酸啤酒風格中，酸味來自細菌，例如乳酸菌，它們在發酵和熟成期間作用，為成品啤酒增加酸度。酒香酵母（Brettanomyces）也可能參與，帶來複雜的農舍、乾草、熟鳳梨和皮革香氣。","Berliner weisse is straw-coloured and hazy, with subtle bread dough from wheat and malt and light fruity notes from fermentation. It is moderately sour, with light body, low alcohol and low or no perceptible bitterness. It is sometimes served with syrups: raspberry or woodruff (a slightly bitter herb reminiscent of sweet hay). It is typically made with cultured yeast and bacteria.":"柏林白啤酒（Berliner weisse）呈稻草色、混濁，帶有小麥和麥芽的細微麵團香，以及發酵帶來的淡淡果香。它適度地酸，酒體輕，酒精低，苦味低或幾乎感覺不到。有時會搭配糖漿飲用：覆盆子或香車葉草（一種微苦、讓人想到甜乾草的香草）。它通常以培養的酵母和細菌釀造。","Sour styles: sourness from bacteria (lactic) during fermentation and maturation":"酸啤酒風格：酸味來自發酵和熟成期間的細菌（乳酸菌）","Sometimes Brett too: farmyard, hay, pineapple, leather":"有時也有 Brett：農舍、乾草、鳳梨、皮革","Berliner weisse: straw, hazy, moderately sour, light, low alcohol":"柏林白啤酒：稻草色、混濁、適度的酸、清淡、酒精低","Sometimes served with raspberry or woodruff syrup; cultured yeast and bacteria":"有時搭配覆盆子或香車葉草糖漿；培養的酵母和細菌","Geuze: spontaneous fermentation":"貴茲：自然發酵","Geuze (gueuze) is gold, with complex farmyard aromas (earth and hay) and fruity ones such as grapefruit, orange, apple, apricot or rhubarb, plus subtle bread crumb. It tastes sour, with little or no bitterness, and its alcohol is medium to high. Bottle-conditioning usually leaves a sediment and gives it plenty of bubbles.":"貴茲（Geuze／gueuze）是金色，帶有複雜的農舍香氣（泥土和乾草），以及葡萄柚、柳橙、蘋果、杏桃或大黃等果香，還有細微的麵包心香。它嘗起來是酸的，苦味很少或沒有，酒精中等到高。瓶中二次發酵通常會留下沉澱，並帶來大量氣泡。","The key difference from Berliner weisse is method: geuze is spontaneously fermented: a mix of ambient yeasts and bacteria, Brettanomyces and lactic acid bacteria among them, gives it its character. Berliner weisse, by contrast, uses cultured yeast and bacteria.":"與柏林白啤酒的關鍵差別在於方法：貴茲是自然發酵的：環境中的酵母和細菌（其中包括酒香酵母和乳酸菌）混合在一起，塑造了它的個性。相反地，柏林白啤酒使用培養的酵母和細菌。","Geuze: gold, sour, farmyard, grapefruit, apple, apricot; low or no bitterness":"貴茲：金色、酸、農舍、葡萄柚、蘋果、杏桃；苦味低或沒有","Medium-high alcohol; sediment, highly carbonated":"酒精中高；有沉澱，碳酸感高","Spontaneous fermentation: ambient yeast and bacteria, including Brett":"自然發酵：環境中的酵母和細菌，包括 Brett","Storing beer":"保存啤酒","Beer starts changing as soon as it is brewed and is easily damaged by oxygen, heat and light. Drink it fresh: some beers benefit from ageing, but most are best young; over time hop aroma and bitterness fade and paper or wet cardboard notes appear. Check for a 'bottled on' or 'best before/use by' date. Keep it cool, ideally refrigerated even for short-term storage: at room temperature it goes stale faster, and warmth degrades it quickly.":"啤酒一釀好就開始變化，很容易受到氧氣、熱和光的損害。要趁新鮮喝：有些啤酒適合陳放，但大多數最好趁年輕喝；隨著時間，啤酒花香氣和苦味會消退，出現紙或濕紙板的調性。注意「裝瓶日期」或「最佳賞味期限／有效期限」。保持涼爽，即使只是短期存放，最好也放冰箱：在室溫下會更快老化，溫熱會讓它迅速劣化。","Protect it from daylight and artificial light, which can create unpleasant aromas known as light strike. Cans and kegs are opaque and protect the beer; brown bottles block almost all damaging light; green or clear bottles give little or no protection and should be stored in sealed boxes. Keep it sealed to protect it from oxygen and keep aromas and carbonation: once opened, bottles and cans should be drunk straight away. Keg beer is packed with carbon dioxide, which protects it from oxygen and keeps it fresh for longer.":"要避開日光和人工光源，它們可能產生稱為光害的難聞香氣。罐和桶不透光，能保護啤酒；棕色瓶能擋住幾乎所有有害的光線；綠色或透明瓶幾乎沒有保護作用，應該放在密封的箱子裡存放。保持密封以隔絕氧氣，保住香氣和碳酸感：瓶裝和罐裝啤酒一旦開啟就應該馬上喝。桶裝啤酒充填了二氧化碳，能隔絕氧氣，保持新鮮較久。","Drink fresh: hops and bitterness fade, cardboard appears; check dates":"趁新鮮喝：啤酒花和苦味消退，出現紙板味；注意日期","Keep cool, ideally refrigerated":"保持涼爽，最好冷藏","Away from light: cans and kegs opaque, brown bottles fine, green or clear in sealed boxes":"避光：罐和桶不透光，棕色瓶可以，綠色或透明瓶放在密封箱中","Sealed: drink at once when opened; CO2-filled kegs stay fresh longer":"密封：開了馬上喝；充填 CO2 的酒桶保鮮較久","Three faults to recognise":"要辨認的三種缺陷","Poor storage or maintenance can cause unpleasant aromas and flavours. Sooner or later most beers go stale, and heat and oxygen make it happen faster: hop aromas and bitterness fade and paper or wet cardboard notes appear. Light strike (skunking) is caused when light hits hop compounds, giving an unpleasant skunky, scorched-hair or cat-urine smell.":"保存或維護不當會造成難聞的香氣和風味。大多數啤酒遲早都會老化，熱和氧氣會讓它來得更快：啤酒花香氣和苦味消退，出現紙或濕紙板的調性。光害（臭鼬味）是光線照到啤酒花成分造成的，會產生難聞的臭鼬味、燒焦頭髮味或貓尿味。","Bacterial infection is commonly caused by bacteria growing in poorly maintained beer lines (the hoses connecting kegs to taps) and gives a mix of unwelcome flavours such as vinegar and rancid butter. Prevention is simple: fresh, cold, dark, sealed beer and clean equipment.":"細菌感染通常是維護不良的啤酒管線（連接酒桶和酒頭的管子）中滋生細菌造成的，會帶來醋和腐敗奶油等不討喜的混合風味。預防很簡單：新鮮、低溫、避光、密封的啤酒，以及乾淨的設備。","Staling: paper, wet cardboard; hops and bitterness faded; heat and oxygen":"老化：紙、濕紙板；啤酒花和苦味消退；熱和氧氣","Light strike: skunky, scorched hair, cat urine; light on hop compounds":"光害：臭鼬味、燒焦頭髮、貓尿；光線照到啤酒花成分","Bacterial infection: vinegar, rancid butter; dirty beer lines":"細菌感染：醋、腐敗奶油；髒的啤酒管線","Glassware and pouring from the keg":"杯具與從酒桶倒酒","There is a huge range of glassware, and personal preference, tradition and culture all matter. For tasting, a few features help: a rounded bowl helps swirling, inward-sloping walls capture aromas, and narrow glasses help head retention. Whatever the shape, the glass must be clean: odourless and free of detergent, dishwasher salts or dirt from unclean cloths. Bubbles clinging to the sides after pouring are a sign the glass is not completely clean.":"杯具種類非常多，個人喜好、傳統和文化都有影響。品飲時，有幾個特點很有幫助：圓弧的杯身方便搖杯，向內傾斜的杯壁能留住香氣，窄的杯子有助於泡沫持久。不論形狀為何，杯子一定要乾淨：沒有氣味，沒有清潔劑、洗碗機鹽或不乾淨抹布留下的髒污。倒酒後氣泡附著在杯壁上，就表示杯子沒有完全洗乾淨。","Pouring keg beer: tilt the glass at 45° under the tap, which must never touch the beer or the glass, and keep your fingers away from the top of the glass. Open the tap fully and pour down the side until the glass is about 70% full. Then bring the glass upright and keep pouring into the centre to form a foam; turn off the tap at the right volume.":"倒桶裝啤酒：把杯子傾斜 45° 放在酒頭下方，酒頭絕不能碰到啤酒或杯子，手指也要遠離杯子上緣。把酒頭完全打開，沿著杯壁倒，直到約七分滿（70%）。然後把杯子立直，繼續往中央倒以形成泡沫；在適當的分量時關掉酒頭。","Rounded bowl: swirling; inward walls: aromas; narrow glass: head retention":"圓弧杯身：方便搖杯；向內的杯壁：留住香氣；窄杯：泡沫持久","Clean glass: clinging bubbles = not clean":"乾淨的杯子：氣泡附著 = 不乾淨","Keg: 45°, tap fully open, down the side to 70%, then upright into the centre":"酒桶：45°，酒頭全開，沿杯壁倒到 70%，再立直往中央倒","The tap never touches beer or glass":"酒頭絕不碰到啤酒或杯子","Bottles, sediment and temperatures":"瓶裝、沉澱與溫度","Opening a crown-capped bottle: steady the bottle with one hand and remove the cap with the opener in one single motion with the other. Pouring: hold the glass at 45° (not touching its upper part) and pour gently down the side; when the glass is 50–70% full, bring it upright and pour into the centre to create foam. With no sediment, pour the whole bottle. With sediment (bottle-conditioned beers), pour carefully, keeping the bottle tilted until the sediment nears the neck, then stop: a little beer always stays in the bottle. Leave the bottle on the table so the drinker can choose to swirl in the sediment. Weissbier and witbier, naturally hazy, are the exception: gently roll the bottle or can before opening and pour everything.":"打開皇冠蓋的瓶子：一手穩住瓶子，另一手用開瓶器以單一動作取下瓶蓋。倒酒：把杯子傾斜 45°（不要碰到杯子上半部），沿著杯壁輕輕倒；杯子到五到七分滿（50–70%）時，把杯子立直，往中央倒以形成泡沫。沒有沉澱的話，就把整瓶倒完。有沉澱的話（瓶中二次發酵的啤酒），要小心倒，保持瓶子傾斜，直到沉澱接近瓶頸時停止：瓶中一定會留下一點啤酒。把瓶子留在桌上，讓飲用者自己選擇是否搖入沉澱。本來就混濁的德式小麥啤酒和比利時白啤酒是例外：開瓶或開罐前輕輕滾動，然後全部倒出。","Personal preference matters a lot for temperature, but there are general rules. Light to medium aroma, low to medium alcohol (international lager, pilsner, weissbier): well chilled, 3–7 °C (37–45 °F). Medium to pronounced aroma, medium to high alcohol (porter, APA, American IPA): chilled, 7–12 °C (45–54 °F). Complex, pronounced aroma, high to very high alcohol (barley wine, dubbel): lightly chilled, 12–15 °C (54–59 °F).":"溫度很大程度取決於個人喜好，但有一般原則。香氣淡到中等、酒精低到中等（國際拉格、皮爾森、德式小麥啤酒）：充分冰鎮，3–7 °C（37–45 °F）。香氣中等到明顯、酒精中等到高（波特、APA、美式 IPA）：冰涼，7–12 °C（45–54 °F）。香氣複雜而明顯、酒精高到非常高（大麥酒、比利時雙料）：微涼，12–15 °C（54–59 °F）。","Crown cap: steady bottle, one single motion":"皇冠蓋：穩住瓶子，單一動作","Bottle: 45°, down the side, at 50–70% upright and pour into the centre":"瓶裝：45°，沿杯壁倒，到 50–70% 時立直往中央倒","With sediment: stop when it reaches the neck; leave bottle on table; weissbier/witbier: roll and pour all":"有沉澱：到瓶頸時停止；瓶子留在桌上；德式小麥／比利時白啤酒：滾動後全部倒出","3–7 °C lager, pilsner, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel":"3–7 °C 拉格、皮爾森、德式小麥啤酒 · 7–12 °C 波特、APA、IPA · 12–15 °C 大麥酒、比利時雙料","Preferences and primary interactions":"喜好與主要交互作用","People differ in their sensitivity to tastes and aromas: a match one person loves can leave another indifferent or even disappointed, so a pairing should start from the individual's own preferences and sensitivities. Food always influences how a drink tastes; how much depends on the person and on the level of the interacting elements. These are principles of perception rather than 'rules'.":"每個人對味道和香氣的敏感度不同：一個人喜愛的搭配，可能讓另一個人無感甚至失望，所以搭配應該從個人自己的喜好和敏感度出發。食物一定會影響飲料的味道；影響多少取決於個人以及交互作用元素的強弱。這些是感知的原則，而不是「規則」。","Primary interactions on beer. Sweetness in food: beer seems less sweet, more acidic and more bitter. Umami: the same, less sweet, more acidic and more bitter. Acidity in food: beer seems sweeter, less acidic and less bitter. Salt: the same, sweeter, less acidic and less bitter. Also, chilli heat increases the perception of alcohol, and bitterness in food increases bitterness in the beer.":"對啤酒的主要交互作用。食物中的甜味：啤酒顯得較不甜、更酸、更苦。鮮味：一樣，較不甜、更酸、更苦。食物中的酸味：啤酒顯得更甜、較不酸、較不苦。鹹味：一樣，更甜、較不酸、較不苦。此外，辣椒的辣度會提高酒精感，食物中的苦味會增加啤酒的苦味。","Personal preferences and sensitivities first":"個人喜好和敏感度優先","Sweet and umami food: beer less sweet, more acidic, more bitter":"甜的和鮮味的食物：啤酒較不甜、更酸、更苦","Acid and salt food: beer sweeter, less acidic, less bitter":"酸的和鹹的食物：啤酒更甜、較不酸、較不苦","Chilli: more perceived alcohol; bitter food: more bitter beer":"辣椒：酒精感更強；苦的食物：啤酒更苦","Sensitive styles, intensity and aromas":"敏感的風格、強度與香氣","Beers are generally very food-friendly, but some styles interact more. High-bitterness styles such as American IPA can seem even more bitter with sweetness, umami or bitterness in the food. High-acidity styles such as geuze can seem even more acidic with sweetness or umami. Strong styles (high or very high alcohol) such as barley wine and tripel make the burn of chilli clearly stronger.":"啤酒一般非常適合配餐，但有些風格的交互作用更明顯。美式 IPA 這類高苦味風格，遇到食物中的甜味、鮮味或苦味可能顯得更苦。貴茲這類高酸度風格，遇到甜味或鮮味可能顯得更酸。大麥酒和比利時三料這類烈的風格（酒精高或非常高），會明顯加強辣椒的灼熱感。","Two other considerations. Intensity: dish and beer should have a similar flavour intensity, or one will overpower the other. Aromas: beers recall many foods (bread, honey, chocolate and coffee from malt; fruit, tea and herbs from hops; fruit and spice from yeast). Looking for similar or complementary aromas in beer and food creates a familiar connection and can lead to wonderful pairings, such as a chocolatey stout with a cocoa dessert.":"另外還有兩個考量。強度：菜餚和啤酒的風味強度應該相近，否則一方會壓過另一方。香氣：啤酒讓人想到許多食物（麥芽帶來麵包、蜂蜜、巧克力和咖啡；啤酒花帶來水果、茶和香草；酵母帶來水果和辛香）。在啤酒和食物中尋找相似或互補的香氣，能建立熟悉的連結，帶來美妙的搭配，例如巧克力風味的司陶特配可可甜點。","High bitterness (American IPA): worse with sweet, umami, bitter":"高苦味（美式 IPA）：遇到甜、鮮味、苦會更糟","High acidity (geuze): worse with sweet and umami":"高酸度（貴茲）：遇到甜和鮮味會更糟","High alcohol (barley wine, tripel): more chilli burn":"高酒精（大麥酒、比利時三料）：辣椒灼熱感更強","Similar intensity; similar or complementary aromas":"強度相近；香氣相似或互補","Malt, water, hops, yeast.":"麥芽、水、啤酒花、酵母。","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + CO2 + aromas.":"糖 + 酵母 → 酒精 + CO2 + 香氣。","Beer alcohol scale":"啤酒酒精分級","Low ≤4% · medium 4.1–5.9% · high 6–9% · very high >9%.":"低 ≤4% · 中等 4.1–5.9% · 高 6–9% · 非常高 >9%。","Starch conversion":"澱粉轉化","Malt enzymes break starch into fermentable sugars.":"麥芽的酵素把澱粉分解成可發酵的糖。","Steeping → germination → kilning.":"浸麥 → 發芽 → 烘麥。","Base malts":"基礎麥芽","Kilned low, enzymes intact; bread, cracker, honey; straw/gold.":"低溫烘麥，酵素完好；麵包、餅乾、蜂蜜；稻草色／金色。","Speciality malts":"特殊麥芽","Hotter kilning or roasting; biscuit, caramel, coffee, chocolate; amber to black.":"較高溫烘麥或烘烤；餅乾、焦糖、咖啡、巧克力；琥珀色到黑色。","Grain bill":"穀物配方","Recipe of malts and grains: mostly base malt + a little speciality malt.":"麥芽和穀物的配方：主要是基礎麥芽 + 少量特殊麥芽。","Milled malt.":"碾磨過的麥芽。","Mash · wort · spent grains":"糖化醪 · 麥汁 · 麥渣","Grist + hot water · separated sugary liquid · leftover solids.":"碎麥芽 + 熱水 · 分離出的含糖液體 · 剩下的固體。","Wort boiling":"麥汁煮沸","Kills microorganisms; main hop additions; then rapid cooling.":"殺死微生物；主要的啤酒花添加；接著快速冷卻。","Bottle-conditioning":"瓶中二次發酵","Further fermentation in the sealed bottle; leaves yeast sediment.":"在密封的瓶中再次發酵；留下酵母沉澱。","Hops: most common form":"啤酒花：最常見的形式","Pellets of dried, milled, pressed cones, kept cold.":"乾燥、碾碎、壓製的毬花顆粒，低溫保存。","German, Czech, British hops":"德國、捷克、英國啤酒花","Subtle: spicy, floral, herbal, earthy, fruity.":"細微：辛香、花香、草本、泥土、果香。","US, NZ, Australian hops":"美國、紐西蘭、澳洲啤酒花","Intense: citrus, stone fruit, tropical, pine.":"強烈：柑橘、核果、熱帶、松木。","Early / late hops / dry hopping":"初期／後段加入／乾投","Start of boil = bitterness; end = aroma; later, cool = aroma.":"煮沸開始 = 苦味；結束 = 香氣；更晚、較涼 = 香氣。","Ale yeast":"艾爾酵母","Quick, warmer, fruity and spicy aromas, many strains → ales.":"快、較溫暖、果香和辛香、菌株多 → 艾爾。","Slower, cooler, less aroma, fewer strains → lagers.":"較慢、較涼、香氣較少、菌株較少 → 拉格。","Yeast: ripe pineapple, peach, farmyard, leather, hay, earth.":"酵母：熟鳳梨、桃子、農舍、皮革、乾草、泥土。","No cultured yeast or bacteria: only ambient ones.":"沒有培養的酵母或細菌：只用環境中的。","Beer appearance":"啤酒的外觀","Clear–hazy–opaque; straw → black; foam.":"清澈–混濁–不透明；稻草色 → 黑色；泡沫。","Yeast aromas":"酵母香氣","Fruit (banana…), spice (clove, pepper), farmyard, bubblegum, nail varnish.":"水果（香蕉…）、辛香（丁香、胡椒）、農舍、泡泡糖、去光水。","American/international pale lager":"美式／國際淡色拉格","Straw-gold, light aroma, low-medium bitterness, medium alcohol, high carbonation.":"稻草色到金色，香氣淡，苦味中低，酒精中等，碳酸感高。","Gold lager, bread crumb, subtle hops; low-medium bitterness. 'Hell' = pale.":"金色拉格，麵包心，細微的啤酒花；苦味中低。「Hell」= 淡色。","Easy straw-gold ale, subtle crumb, medium bitterness; also golden ale.":"易飲的稻草色到金色艾爾，細微的麵包心香，苦味中等；也稱 golden ale。","Copper-brown lager, toast, nut; 'dunkel' = dark.":"銅色到棕色的拉格，烤麵包、堅果；「dunkel」= 深色。","Brown or black ales, coffee and chocolate; 'imperial' = very high alcohol.":"棕色或黑色的艾爾，咖啡和巧克力；「imperial」（帝國）= 酒精非常高。","Often amber ale, intense malt, full, sweet, high/very high alcohol; ages well.":"常為琥珀色艾爾，麥芽香濃烈，飽滿，甜，酒精高／非常高；適合陳放。","Czech or German pilsner":"捷克或德國皮爾森","Straw-gold lager, subtle spicy-floral hops, medium-high bitterness.":"稻草色到金色的拉格，細微的辛香、花香啤酒花，苦味中高。","English amber-copper ale, biscuit/caramel, subtle hops, medium-high bitterness.":"英國琥珀色到銅色的艾爾，餅乾／焦糖，細微的啤酒花，苦味中高。","Medium-high bitterness · high bitterness, stronger · hazy, less bitter.":"苦味中高 · 苦味高、更烈 · 混濁、苦味較低。","Hazy, banana and clove, wheat, low bitterness, highly carbonated.":"混濁，香蕉和丁香，小麥，苦味低，碳酸感高。","Hazy, coriander and orange peel, wheat, low bitterness.":"混濁，芫荽和橙皮，小麥，苦味低。","Dubbel copper-brown, high alcohol; tripel gold, even higher alcohol.":"比利時雙料銅色到棕色，酒精高；三料金色，酒精更高。","Gold-amber, orange, peach, pepper; can be slightly sour.":"金色到琥珀色，柳橙、桃子、胡椒；可能帶輕微酸味。","Straw, hazy, moderately sour, low alcohol; cultured yeast and bacteria.":"稻草色、混濁、適度的酸、酒精低；培養的酵母和細菌。","Gold, sour, farmyard and fruit; spontaneous fermentation; highly carbonated.":"金色、酸、農舍和果香；自然發酵；碳酸感高。","Four storage rules":"保存的四個原則","Drink fresh, keep cool, protect from light, keep sealed.":"趁新鮮喝、保持涼爽、避光、保持密封。","Faded hops and bitterness, paper or wet cardboard; heat and oxygen.":"啤酒花和苦味消退，紙或濕紙板味；熱和氧氣。","Light strike (skunking)":"光害（臭鼬味）","Light on hop compounds: skunky, scorched hair, cat urine.":"光線照到啤酒花成分：臭鼬味、燒焦頭髮、貓尿。","Bacterial infection":"細菌感染","Dirty beer lines: vinegar, rancid butter.":"髒的啤酒管線：醋、腐敗奶油。","Bottles and light":"酒瓶與光線","Brown: almost full protection; green or clear: little or none.":"棕色：幾乎完全保護；綠色或透明：幾乎沒有保護。","Pouring keg beer":"倒桶裝啤酒","45°, tap fully open, down the side to 70%, then upright into the centre.":"45°，酒頭全開，沿杯壁倒到 70%，再立直往中央倒。","Beer with sediment":"有沉澱的啤酒","Pour gently, stop when sediment reaches the neck; leave bottle on the table.":"輕輕倒，沉澱到瓶頸時停止；瓶子留在桌上。","3–7 °C lager, pilsner, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel.":"3–7 °C 拉格、皮爾森、德式小麥啤酒 · 7–12 °C 波特、APA、IPA · 12–15 °C 大麥酒、比利時雙料。","Sweet and umami food":"甜的和鮮味的食物","Beer less sweet, more acidic, more bitter.":"啤酒較不甜、更酸、更苦。","Acid and salt food":"酸的和鹹的食物","Beer sweeter, less acidic, less bitter.":"啤酒更甜、較不酸、較不苦。","Food-sensitive styles":"對食物敏感的風格","American IPA (bitterness), geuze (acidity), barley wine and tripel (alcohol with chilli).":"美式 IPA（苦味）、貴茲（酸度）、大麥酒和比利時三料（酒精遇上辣椒）。"});(window.TWG_I18N_F=window.TWG_I18N_F||{})["zh-hant/b1"]=1;
